ed on the human colonic microbiota and its association with diet.HOLD GL:Hold GL is a researcher focused on the role of gut microbiota in inflammatory bowel disease. They have conducted studies exploring how gut microbiota contributes to the pathogenesis of this condition, aiming to deepen the understanding of its implications in inflammatory bowel disease.SMITH M:Smith M is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of gut microbiota in inflammatory bowel disease.GRANGE C:Grange C is a researcher studying the role of gut microbiota in disease pathogenesis.WATT ER:Watt ER is a researcher involved in the study of gut microbiota and its implications for health.EL-OMAR EM:El-Omar EM is a researcher focused on the role of gut microbiota in inflammatory bowel disease.MUKHOPADHYA I:Mukhopadhya I is a researcher studying the gut microbiota's role in disease.TURNBAUGH P:Turnbaugh P is a researcher who has studied the effect of diet on the human gut microbiome.RIDAURA V:Ridaura V is a researcher involved in the metagenomic analysis of the human gut microbiome.FAITH J:Faith J is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of the human gut microbiome.REY F:Rey F is a researcher studying the effects of diet on gut microbiota.GORDON J:Gordon J is a researcher focused on the relationship between diet and the human gut microbiome.ZHANG H:Zhang H is a researcher and co-author known for contributions to the field of surgery and obesity research. They co-authored a study published in the International Journal of Surgery, which examined the effect of early oral feeding on the short-term outcomes of patients undergoing laparoscopic distal gastrectomy. Additionally, Zhang H has conducted research on the human gut microbiota, focusing on its role in obesity and the changes that occur following gastric bypass surgery.DIBAISE JK:DiBaise JK is a researcher involved in the study of gut microbiota and obesity.ZUCCOLO A:Zuccolo A is a researcher who has contributed to the 