º‘såΩ ﬁ"<ÙÕ¥∫°Ω©≥Ω•Àäº˚»ªí7ùª—ôWºÖ»~ªøºîºÜ®;@ä ;ù˚íºú¥ªò-‡ª™Ÿºú*ü:˚©Æ<i¥ÍªŒ∆ûªä≈Ωº√”ú<YÀ•;~ﬁ=∫(—ºø÷›;~Q=¯BUºm>N=πß<»å="$ ;®+h;{wdºMµ∫vÅ!=ö6!º‚¨¢ºä	º´ßΩø≠<Â∏<†[ª˚»∫4ﬂ;?∫0°Ö<•X/º6◊ªH+∂ºñN•º[ÓØ;∫Lz<Mµ:b}º´÷ê<`‰Úºπ‡ö<U¥ù<|å'<™Y<ØK1<a&º—ô◊ºå[#<Bmºı;w≤;cÌ3<‹rêºFï–ªw1–:˜cö<S¿üºW¥ºcÌ≥º›Ø„ª‚¨¢<WJΩWJÉºıÑºWy<xu<ˆæ<√§ê;Ñ˛Ü<ñ¨=ºDC∫º˚©ÆºÓì"ºVìÿ=4âÅ<J}LΩ@˝•:b˝;DÂ°∫≈%3<UVº‹–(<ÿF≈ª•)#=Ï“ªeTç;Wy=Ë*ΩàDõº>8¥ºœG¡<DÂ°ªÃºº2ƒΩJ9}<Ë*Ñ;D.˜º˘Wò;sº/ºqÑ‚º©Ω‘DÄ∫␀Õº“PÇº30Ô∫r;Ωó¡␀=~Ä•<DÂ!ºÇı≈ºÏpΩ[ø£ªäRb<å[#<≥¶=Ø%ªàs'ºc©‰<8œ=ZŸÏºíÄÚ;Qùºrjôº‡Á0<!mu<‹ˇ4<ú\<690<8ÎºFŸ<∑yª’Å”ªÄEóº–5<Äã<r›<Ë∑®;ﬁféª{"title": "FUSOBACTERIUM:Fusobacterium is a genus of bacteria that belongs to the phylum Fusobacteria. It is commonly found as part of the normal flora in the human mouth and gut. While many species of Fusobacterium coexist harmlessly within these environments, some are associated with various diseases. This dual role highlights the complexity of Fusobacterium, as it can contribute to both health and disease states in humans."}{"title": "PEPTOSTREPTOCOCCUS:Peptostreptococcus is a genus of bacteria within the phylum Firmicutes, significant in the context of human health."}{"title": "RUMINOCOCCUS:Ruminococcus is a genus of bacteria belonging to the phylum Firmicutes. This genus is recognized for its significant role in the fermentation of dietary fibers, contributing to the digestive processes in various organisms. Additionally, Ruminococcus has been associated with decreased amounts in obese individuals, suggesting a potential link between its presence and body weight regulation."}{"title": "BIFIDOBACTERIUM:Bifidobacterium is a genus of bacteria that plays a crucial role in promoting gut health. It is commonly found in the intestines and is known for its beneficial effects, including the modulation of inflammation and metabolic processes. Research has shown that Bifidobacterium is negatively correlated with obesity and diabetes, with lower quantities of this bacterium observed in obese individuals. This genus is frequently utilized in probiotic treatments, highlighting its importance in maintaining a healthy gut microbiome. Bifidobacterium belongs to the phylum Actinobacteria and is recognized for its contributions to overall gut health, making it a significant focus of studies related to obesity and metabolic health."}{"title": "PROTEOBACTERIA:Proteobacteria is a major phylum of bacteria that encompasses a diverse range of pathogens and plays a significant role in the context of gut microbiota. Research studies have indicated that Proteobacteria can exhibit changes in response to antibiotic administration, highlighting its dynamic nature and importance in microbial ecology and health."}{"title": "FILO: FIRMICUTES:"}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS AFRICANOS:Grupo de ni\u00f1os que presentan una microbiota intestinal rica en Bacteroidetes y con una mayor riqueza microbiana en comparaci\u00f3n con los ni\u00f1os europeos, debido a su dieta alta en fibra y baja en grasas animales."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS EUROPEOS:Grupo de ni\u00f1os que presentan una microbiota intestinal caracterizada por una mayor proporci\u00f3n de Firmicutes y una menor riqueza microbiana, atribuida a su dieta alta en grasas y prote\u00ednas de origen animal y baja en fibra."}{"title": "DIETA ALTA EN FIBRA:Patr\u00f3n diet\u00e9tico que se asocia con un aumento en la proporci\u00f3n de Bacteroidetes y una disminuci\u00f3n en Firmicutes en la microbiota intestinal."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES DE LA ENERG\u00cdA:Bloque que describe c\u00f3mo los cambios en la dieta afectan la microbiota intestinal y la energ\u00eda del cuerpo."}{"title": "PATRONES DIET\u00c9TICOS:Factores que influyen en la composici\u00f3n de la microbiota intestinal, mostrando diferencias significativas entre grupos con h\u00e1bitos diet\u00e9ticos diferentes."}{"title": "MICROBIOTA DE COMUNIDADES OCCIDENTALES:Descripci\u00f3n de la microbiota intestinal de comunidades occidentales, caracterizada por una ingesta alta en grasa y prote\u00ednas de origen animal y un bajo contenido en fibra."}{"title": "MICROBIOTA DE COMUNIDADES ORIENTALES:Descripci\u00f3n de la microbiota intestinal de comunidades orientales, que muestra una mayor riqueza microbiana y una mayor proporci\u00f3n de Bacteroidetes."}{"title": "DIETA ALTA EN GRASAS:"}{"title": "BACTERIANA:Bacteriana is a research entity focused on the study of intestinal microbiota and its relation to obesity and metabolic diseases."}{"title": "AKKERMANSIA MUCINIPHILA:Akkermansia muciniphila is a beneficial bacterium that plays a significant role in gut health and metabolic processes. This species of bacteria is known for its ability to degrade mucin, a component of the mucus layer in the gut, and is linked to improved metabolic profiles, particularly in relation to obesity and diabetes. Research indicates that higher levels of Akkermansia muciniphila correlate with better metabolic health outcomes in rodents, especially when its abundance is normalized through dietary changes and prebiotic intake.\n\nInterestingly, Akkermansia muciniphila can also increase in abundance following broad-spectrum antibiotic treatment, which may have implications for reducing the incidence of diabetes. Overall, this bacterium is associated with the gut microbiota and is considered important for metabolic health, with potential applications in obesity prevention and treatment."}{"title": "ENDOTOXEMIA METAB\u00d3LICA:Endotoxemia metab\u00f3lica refers to the presence of endotoxins in the bloodstream, often linked to inflammation and metabolic disorders."}{"title": "S\u00cdNTESIS DE \u00c1CIDOS GRASOS DE CADENA CORTA:Synthesis of short-chain fatty acids (SCFA) is a metabolic process that occurs in the gut, associated with various health benefits including improved gut health and reduced inflammation."}{"title": "MICROBIOTA:Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms, including bacteria, that inhabit various environments within the human body, with a significant concentration residing in the gut. This community plays a vital role in several aspects of health, including digestion, metabolism, and the development of allergic diseases. The composition of the microbiota can be influenced by various factors, such as antibiotic use, which can alter its balance. Additionally, the microbiota is notably affected in conditions like obesity, where it can impact metabolic functions and contribute to the overall health of an individual."}{"title": "NEYRINCK:Neyrinck is a researcher who studied the effects of broad-spectrum antibiotics on obese rodents and their metabolic alterations."}{"title": "DEKZENNE:Dekzenne is a researcher who collaborated with Neyrinck in studying the effects of antibiotics on the microbiota of obese rodents."}{"title": "CANI:Cani is a researcher who supports the idea that broad-spectrum antibiotic therapy significantly reduces plasma levels of lipopolysaccharides in animal models."}{"title": "MEMBREZ:Membrez is a researcher who studied the effects of antibiotic treatment on genetically obese rodents with insulin resistance."}{"title": "H. PYLORI:H. pylori, or Helicobacter pylori, is a bacterium that can infect humans, particularly the stomach. It is often associated with various gastrointestinal diseases, including ulcers, and has implications for iron absorption. Additionally, H. pylori has been mentioned in the context of antibiotic exposure, which may influence weight gain. This bacterium plays a significant role in gastrointestinal health and disease, highlighting its importance in medical research and treatment."}{"title": "ANTIBIOTIC THERAPY:Antibiotic therapy is a treatment method employed to combat bacterial infections, frequently initiated empirically in severe cases. This approach involves the use of antibiotics to address infections and has been the subject of research regarding its effects on microbiota and potential weight gain."}{"title": "INFECCIONES BACTERIANAS:Infecciones bacterianas refer to bacterial infections that antibiotics are used to treat, which can impact microbiota diversity."}{"title": "ALERGIAS:Alergias refer to allergies, which are immune system reactions to specific substances. These reactions can be influenced by various factors, including genetic predispositions and environmental conditions. Additionally, changes in microbiota due to antibiotic use may also play a role in the development of allergies. Among the different types of allergies, food allergies are notable as they represent adverse immune responses to certain foods. These food allergies can manifest in early childhood and may vary in duration and severity over time."}{"title": "DIVERSIDAD FILOGEN\u00c9TICA:Diversidad filogen\u00e9tica refers to the genetic diversity of microbial communities, which can be altered by antibiotic treatment."}{"title": "SISTEMA INMUNE:El sistema inmune es el conjunto de c\u00e9lulas y mecanismos que protegen al organismo contra infecciones y enfermedades, incluyendo reacciones al\u00e9rgicas. Este sistema es fundamental para la defensa del cuerpo y su desarrollo en ni\u00f1os puede influir en la prevalencia de alergias. Adem\u00e1s, el sistema inmune es una red compleja de c\u00e9lulas y prote\u00ednas que defiende al organismo contra infecciones, y su desarrollo y mantenimiento est\u00e1n influenciados por la microbiota intestinal. Cambios en esta microbiota, como los provocados por el uso de antibi\u00f3ticos, pueden afectar el funcionamiento del sistema inmune."}{"title": "ROEDORES:"}{"title": "GENES CANDIDATOS:Los genes candidatos son aquellos identificados en estudios de asociaci\u00f3n que ayudan a entender la sensibilidad y resistencia a la diabetes y obesidad."}{"title": "DIVERSIDAD GEN\u00c9TICA:La diversidad gen\u00e9tica se refiere a las variaciones en los genes entre individuos, lo que puede influir en la susceptibilidad a enfermedades metab\u00f3licas."}{"title": "FACTORES AMBIENTALES:Los factores ambientales son condiciones externas que pueden afectar la salud, incluyendo la dieta y el estilo de vida, y est\u00e1n relacionados con el aumento de la obesidad."}{"title": "BUTIRATO:Butirato, also known as butyrate, is a short-chain fatty acid produced by gut bacteria during the fermentation of dietary fiber. It plays a crucial role in energy metabolism by providing energy to colon epithelial cells and reducing intestinal permeability. Additionally, butirato is involved in the apoptosis of inflammatory cells and enhances the function of the mucosal barrier, contributing to inflammation reduction and overall gut health."}{"title": "LIPOPOLISAC\u00c1RIDOS:Lipopolysaccharides (LPS) are pro-inflammatory components found in the cell wall of gram-negative bacteria. They are associated with increased intestinal permeability and are linked to chronic inflammation, which is often related to obesity."}{"title": "GHRLINA:Ghrelin is a hormone that stimulates appetite, its levels are influenced by gut microbiota composition and dietary intake."}{"title": "BIFIDOBACTERIAS:Bifidobacteria are beneficial gut bacteria that play a crucial role in digestion and maintaining gut health. They are associated with lower levels of ghrelin, a hormone that regulates appetite. These bacteria are typically found in the intestines and their populations can be increased by diets rich in prebiotics, which support their growth and activity. Overall, Bifidobacteria contribute positively to digestive health and metabolic regulation."}{"title": "LACTOBACILUS:Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria that is part of the gut microbiota, known for its role in fermenting carbohydrates and producing beneficial metabolites."}{"title": "BLOQUE: ALTERACIONES DE LA ENERG\u00cdA:This section discusses the alterations in energy balance related to dietary interventions and their effects on host metabolism."}{"title": "NFKB:NFKB, also known as nuclear factor kappa-light-chain-enhancer of activated B cells, is a protein complex that plays a crucial role in regulating immune response and inflammation. It is essential for controlling the transcription of DNA, thereby influencing the immune response to infections. Through its regulatory functions, NFKB is integral to the body's ability to respond to various immune challenges."}{"title": "TLR4:Toll-like receptor 4 (TLR4) is a protein that plays a crucial role in the immune system by recognizing pathogens and activating inflammatory responses."}{"title": "MACR\u00d3FAGO:Macrophages are immune cells that engulf and digest cellular debris and pathogens, playing a vital role in the immune response and inflammation."}{"title": "FIAF:FIAF, or fat-induced adipocyte factor, is a gene expressed in the intestine that plays a crucial role in regulating fat metabolism. It inhibits lipoprotein lipase activity, which in turn affects fat storage in both the liver and adipose tissue. Additionally, FIAF is a protein that is influenced by the gut microbiota, highlighting its connection to the body's metabolic processes and the impact of intestinal health on fat regulation."}{"title": "ACIDOS BILIARES:Bile acids are produced in the liver and play a role in fat digestion and metabolism, with primary and secondary forms affecting energy expenditure."}{"title": "RECEPTOR TOLL-LIKE 4:TLR4 is a receptor that recognizes lipopolysaccharides from gram-negative bacteria, activating inflammatory pathways."}{"title": "PROBIOTICOS:Probiotics are beneficial bacteria that can modulate gut microbiota composition and enhance butyrate production."}{"title": "GLP-2:GLP-2, or glucagon-like peptide-2, is a hormone peptide that plays a crucial role in promoting intestinal growth and protecting against intestinal atrophy. This peptide hormone is integral to the regulation of gut function and energy homeostasis, working in conjunction with GLP-1 to support these processes. Overall, GLP-2 is essential for maintaining intestinal health and functionality."}{"title": "PYY:PYY (peptide YY) is an intestinal hormone that helps regulate appetite and energy balance."}{"title": "YADAV ET AL:Yadav et al are researchers who demonstrated the modulation of intestinal microbiota composition through probiotics, stimulating butyrate production and improving inflammatory status and insulin resistance."}{"title": "PEPTIDO INTESTINAL YY:Peptido intestinal YY is a hormone involved in reducing appetite and regulating energy balance."}{"title": "SCFA:Short-chain fatty acids (SCFA) are fatty acids characterized by having fewer than six carbon atoms. They are produced during the fermentation of dietary fibers in the gut by gut bacteria. SCFAs play a crucial role in maintaining gut health, contributing to various physiological processes and overall well-being."}{"title": "GPR43:GPR43 is a G protein-coupled receptor that mediates the effects of SCFA on glucose metabolism and appetite regulation."}{"title": "GPR41:GPR41 is a G protein-coupled receptor that is involved in the signaling pathways activated by SCFA."}{"title": "GORDON ET AL:Gordon et al are researchers who studied the effects of microbial colonization on body weight and fat in germ-free mice."}{"title": "B\u00c4CKHED ET AL:B\u00e4ckhed et al are researchers who contributed to the understanding of the relationship between gut microbiota and obesity."}{"title": "ACTINOBACTERIA:Actinobacteria is a phylum of bacteria that has been linked to obesity, showing increased representation in obese individuals."}{"title": "POLISAC\u00c1RIDOS INDIGERIBLES:Indigestible polysaccharides are substances that require microbiota to convert them into absorbable monosaccharides and short-chain fatty acids (SCFA), playing a role in energy extraction."}{"title": "M. SMITHII:M. smithii is a type of Archaea that converts hydrogen into methane, playing a role in the digestion of indigestible polysaccharides."}{"title": "RUMINCOCCUS:"}{"title": "TURNBAUGH PJ:Turnbaugh PJ is a prominent researcher recognized for his significant contributions to the understanding of the human microbiome and its impact on health. He has conducted important experiments that demonstrate the causal relationship between microbiota and obesity, highlighting how microbial ecology is associated with this condition. Through his work, Turnbaugh PJ has advanced the field of microbiome research, particularly in relation to its implications for obesity and overall health."}{"title": "AKKERMANSIA:Akkermansia is a genus of bacteria that has been associated with gut health and obesity."}{"title": "RATONES:Experiments involving mice were conducted to study the effects of microbiota on obesity."}{"title": "GEMELOS HOMOCIG\u00d3TICOS DISCORDANTES:Gemelos homocig\u00f3ticos discordantes son gemelos que tienen diferentes caracter\u00edsticas de obesidad, utilizados en estudios sobre microbiota y obesidad."}{"title": "RATONES GEN\u00c9TICAMENTE ID\u00c9NTICOS:Rats that are genetically identical used in experiments to study the effects of diet on microbiota and obesity."}{"title": "LACTOBACILLUS RHAMNOSUS:Lactobacillus rhamnosus is a specific strain of Lactobacillus that has shown beneficial effects on obesity."}{"title": "LACTOBACILLUS GASSERI:Lactobacillus gasseri is another strain of Lactobacillus that has demonstrated positive effects on obesity and metabolic health."}{"title": "ACINETOBACTER:Acinetobacter is a genus of bacteria known for its role in causing infections, particularly in healthcare settings, where it poses a significant risk to patients with invasive devices. In addition to its pathogenic potential, Acinetobacter has been positively associated with obesity and has been the subject of research concerning metabolic health and obesity. This dual role highlights the importance of understanding Acinetobacter not only as a potential infectious agent but also in the context of metabolic disorders."}{"title": "ALIIVIBRIO:Aliivibrio is a genus of bacteria that has been positively associated with obesity and may have implications for gut health. This connection suggests that Aliivibrio could play a significant role in understanding the relationship between gut microbiota and obesity, highlighting its potential importance in studies related to metabolic health and dietary impacts."}{"title": "MARINOMONAS:Marinomonas is a genus of bacteria that has been positively associated with obesity and has been studied for its potential effects on health. This genus is of interest in the field of microbiology due to its implications in understanding the relationship between gut microbiota and metabolic conditions."}{"title": "PSEUDOALTEROMONAS:Pseudoalteromonas is a genus of bacteria that has garnered attention for its potential implications in health and disease. Notably, it has been positively associated with obesity, suggesting a significant role in metabolic processes. Research surrounding Pseudoalteromonas continues to explore its various effects on human health, highlighting its importance in understanding the complex interactions between gut microbiota and overall well-being."}{"title": "KALLIOM\u00c4KI ET AL:Kalliom\u00e4ki et al conducted a study showing a higher proportion of Bifidobacterium and lower Staphylococcus aureus in normal-weight children compared to those who developed overweight over the years."}{"title": "GAMMAPROTEOBACTERIA:Gammaproteobacteria is a class of bacteria that showed significant increase in subjects after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "MICROBIOME:Microbiome refers to the collective genomes of the microbiota, influencing energy absorption and nutrient deposition in the host."}{"title": "SHEWANELLA:Shewanella is a genus of bacteria that has been positively associated with obesity."}{"title": "LACHNOSPIRA:Lachnospira is a genus of bacteria that has been positively associated with obesity."}{"title": "CITOBACTER:Citrobacter is a genus of bacteria that has been positively associated with obesity."}{"title": "SHIGELLA:Shigella is a genus of bacteria known for causing bacillary dysentery, which is characterized by diarrhea that contains blood and mucus. Additionally, Shigella has been positively associated with obesity, indicating a potential link between this bacterial genus and weight-related health issues."}{"title": "PARABACTEROIDES DISTASONIS:Parabacteroides distasonis is a species of bacteria that has been positively associated with obesity."}{"title": "E. COLI:E. coli, or Escherichia coli, is a species of bacteria that has a complex relationship with human health. It has been positively associated with obesity, indicating that certain strains may play a role in weight regulation. Additionally, some strains of E. coli can be utilized as probiotics, contributing to gut health by promoting a balanced microbiome. This dual nature highlights the importance of distinguishing between different strains of E. coli, as their effects on health can vary significantly."}{"title": "PREVOTELLA:Prevotella is a genus of bacteria that has been negatively associated with obesity."}{"title": "SUTTERELLA:Sutterella is a genus of bacteria that has been negatively associated with obesity."}{"title": "METHANOBREVIPA:Methanobrevibacter is a genus of bacteria that has been negatively associated with obesity."}{"title": "LACTOBACILLUS REUTERI:Lactobacillus reuteri is a type of beneficial bacteria that is found in the gut microbiota. It has been associated with various studies related to obesity, highlighting its potential role in influencing metabolic health and weight management."}{"title": "HUMAN GUT:The human gut is the digestive tract where the microbiota resides and plays a significant role in nutrient absorption and metabolism."}{"title": "STOMBAUGH JI:Stombaugh JI is a co-author of a study on the diversity of the human intestinal microbial flora published in Science."}{"title": "GORDON JI:Gordon JI is a researcher dedicated to exploring the role of gut microbes in human health and obesity. He has made significant contributions to the understanding of host-bacterial mutualism within the human intestine, highlighting the intricate relationships between humans and their gut microbiota. Through his work, Gordon JI aims to shed light on how these microbial communities influence various aspects of health, particularly in relation to obesity."}{"title": "JANSSON JK:Jansson JK is a co-author of research on the human gut microbiota."}{"title": "KNIGHT R:Knight R is a researcher recognized for his significant contributions to the study of microbial communities and their diversity. He has a particular focus on the human gut microbiome, exploring its implications for health and disease. Through his work, Knight R has advanced the understanding of how these microbial populations interact and influence various biological processes."}{"title": "ECKBURG PB:Eckburg PB is a co-author of a study on the diversity of the human intestinal microbial flora."}{"title": "B\u00c4CKHED F:B\u00e4ckhed F is a researcher known for his studies on host-bacterial mutualism in the human intestine. He has also investigated the mechanisms of resistance to diet-induced obesity in germ-free mice, contributing to the understanding of how gut bacteria interact with the host and influence metabolic processes."}{"title": "GUARNER F:Guarner F is a researcher who has written about the role of intestinal flora in health and disease."}{"title": "COSTELLO EK:Costello EK is a researcher who studied bacterial community variation in human body habitats."}{"title": "PETERSON J:Peterson J is a co-author of the NIH Human Microbiome Project study."}{"title": "LOZUPONE CA:"}{"title": "NIH HUMAN MICROBIOME PROJECT:The NIH Human Microbiome Project is a research initiative aimed at understanding the human microbiome and its role in health and disease."}{"title": "META HIT CONSORTIUM:The MetaHIT Consortium is a collaborative research project focused on the human gut microbiome and its genetic diversity."}{"title": "TURNBAUGH, P.J.:P.J. Turnbaugh is a researcher involved in multiple studies related to the human microbiome and its implications for health."}{"title": "HAMADY, M.:M. Hamady is a researcher who has contributed to studies on the human microbiome, particularly in relation to gut health."}{"title": "QIN, J.:J. Qin is a researcher known for his work on the human gut microbial gene catalogue established by metagenomics sequencing."}{"title": "BENSON, A.K.:A.K. Benson is a researcher who has studied the individuality of gut microbiota composition and its genetic influences."}{"title": "KOENIG, J.E.:J.E. Koenig is a researcher focused on the succession of microbial consortia in the developing infant gut microbiome."}{"title": "BURKE, C.:C. Burke is a researcher who has studied bacterial community assembly based on functional genes."}{"title": "ADLERBERTH, I.:I. Adlerberth is a researcher who has investigated the establishment of gut microbiota in Western infants."}{"title": "DOMINGUEZ-BELLO, M.G.:M.G. Dominguez-Bello is a researcher known for her work on how delivery mode shapes the acquisition of microbiota in newborns."}{"title": "HUUURE, A.:A. Huurre is a researcher focused on the study of gut microbiota and its implications for health. Their research includes investigating the effects of different modes of delivery on gut microbiota and immunity, contributing to a deeper understanding of how these factors influence overall health outcomes."}{"title": "GUT MICROBIOME:The gut microbiome refers to the complex community of microorganisms residing in the gastrointestinal tract, which plays a crucial role in human health."}{"title": "NATURE:Nature is a prominent scientific journal recognized for its high-quality research publications across a wide array of fields, including biology, medicine, and environmental sciences. The journal features studies on significant topics such as the gut microbiome and obesity, as well as research focused on the human microbiome. Through its diverse range of articles, Nature contributes to the advancement of scientific knowledge and understanding in various disciplines."}{"title": "PROCEEDINGS OF THE NATIONAL ACADEMY OF SCIENCES:Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences (PNAS) is a scientific journal that publishes research articles, including those related to the human microbiome."}{"title": "ACTA PAEDIATRICA:Acta Paediatrica is a journal that publishes research related to pediatrics, including studies on the establishment of gut microbiota in infants."}{"title": "PLOS BIOLOGY:PLOS Biology is an open-access journal that publishes research articles across all areas of biology, including studies on the development of the human infant intestinal microbiota."}{"title": "APPLIED AND ENVIRONMENTAL MICROBIOLOGY:Applied and Environmental Microbiology is a journal that publishes research on microbiology, including studies on the transmission of gut bacteria from mother to infant."}{"title": "TRENDS IN MICROBIOLOGY:Trends in Microbiology is a journal that publishes reviews and research articles on microbiology, including the development of intestinal microbiota in infants."}{"title": "GENOME BIOLOGY AND EVOLUTION:Genome Biology and Evolution is a journal dedicated to publishing research in the fields of evolutionary biology and genomics. It encompasses a wide range of studies, including those focused on gut microbiota and microbiomes. The journal serves as a platform for disseminating significant findings that contribute to the understanding of evolutionary processes and the genetic underpinnings of various biological phenomena."}{"title": "KALLIOMAKI, M.:M. Kalliomaki is a researcher who has contributed to studies on the gut microbiota and its implications for health."}{"title": "RAUTAVA, S.:S. Rautava is a researcher focused on the impact of delivery mode on gut microbiota and immunity."}{"title": "RINNE, M.:M. Rinne is a researcher who has studied the effects of delivery mode on gut microbiota."}{"title": "SALMINEN:Salminen is a researcher involved in studies on gut microbiota and health outcomes."}{"title": "RAVEL, J.:J. Ravel is a researcher known for work on the vaginal microbiome of reproductive-age women."}{"title": "CLAESSON, M.J.:M.J. Claesson is a researcher who has studied the intestinal microbiota of the elderly."}{"title": "DE FILIPPO, C.:C. De Filippo is a researcher who has investigated the impact of diet on gut microbiota in children."}{"title": "HARAKEH, S.M.:S.M. Harakeh is a researcher studying the relationship between gut microbiota and obesity."}{"title": "SHEN, W.:W. Shen is a researcher focused on the influence of dietary fat on intestinal microbes and health."}{"title": "WU, G.D.:G.D. Wu is a researcher linking dietary patterns with gut microbial enterotypes."}{"title": "CANI, P.D.:P.D. Cani is a researcher studying the role of gut microbiota in energy metabolism and metabolic diseases."}{"title": "EVERARD, A.:A. Everard is a researcher investigating the interaction between Akkermansia muciniphila and intestinal epithelium."}{"title": "UBEDA, C.:C. Ubeda is a researcher studying the effects of antibiotics on microbiota and immune defense."}{"title": "JERNBERG, C.:C. Jernberg is a researcher focused on the ecological impacts of antibiotic administration on gut microbiota."}{"title": "SULLIVAN, A.:A. Sullivan is a researcher examining the effects of antimicrobial agents on human microflora."}{"title": "HANSEN, C.H.F.:C.H.F. Hansen is a researcher studying the effects of early life treatment with vancomycin on gut microbiota."}{"title": "PROCEEDINGS OF THE NATIONAL ACADEMY OF SCIENCES USA:Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences USA is a scientific journal that publishes research articles, including studies on microbiomes and health."}{"title": "FRONTIERS IN CELLULAR AND INFECTION MICROBIOLOGY:Frontiers in Cellular and Infection Microbiology is a journal that focuses on research related to microbiology, including gut microbiota and its implications for health."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF NUTRITION BIOCHEMISTRY:Journal of Nutrition Biochemistry publishes research on the biochemical aspects of nutrition, including studies on dietary impacts on gut microbiota."}{"title": "FEMS MICROBIOLOGY ECOLOGY:FEMS Microbiology Ecology is a journal that publishes research on microbial ecology, including studies on gut microbiota and its role in health."}{"title": "ISME JOURNAL:ISME Journal is a scientific journal that focuses on microbial ecology and evolution, including studies on gut microbiota."}{"title": "LANCET INFECTIOUS DISEASES:Lancet Infectious Diseases is a journal that publishes research on infectious diseases, including studies on the effects of antibiotics on gut microbiota."}{"title": "CURRENT OPINION IN CLINICAL NUTRITION AND METABOLIC CARE:\"Current Opinion in Clinical Nutrition and Metabolic Care\" is a journal dedicated to exploring recent research in the fields of nutrition and metabolism. It covers a wide range of topics, including studies on gut microbiota and their impact on health. The journal also provides comprehensive reviews on current trends in clinical nutrition, ensuring that readers are informed about the latest developments in the field. Additionally, it has published insights into specific areas such as the metabolism of alpha-linolenic acid and its implications for health, further contributing to the understanding of nutritional science."}{"title": "FASEB J:FASEB Journal is a peer-reviewed scientific journal that covers research in the field of biology, particularly related to the Federation of American Societies for Experimental Biology."}{"title": "CLIN MICROBIOL INFECT:Clinical Microbiology and Infection is a journal that publishes articles on clinical microbiology and infectious diseases."}{"title": "INT J OBES:International Journal of Obesity is a journal that focuses on obesity research and its implications."}{"title": "NCD-RISC:The NCD Risk Factor Collaboration is a research collaboration that analyzes trends in non-communicable disease risk factors globally."}{"title": "NOD MOUSE:The NOD mouse is a model used in diabetes research, particularly for studying autoimmune diabetes."}{"title": "GUT:Gut microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms living in the digestive tracts of humans and other animals, which plays a crucial role in health and disease."}{"title": "MICE:Mice are commonly used in scientific research, particularly in studies related to genetics, disease, and treatment effects."}{"title": "CANI PD:Cani PD is a researcher known for significant contributions to the understanding of gut microbiota and its impact on metabolic health. Additionally, Cani PD has explored the role of the endocannabinoid system in relation to gut microbiota and adipogenesis, further enhancing the knowledge in this field."}{"title": "MILLION M:Million M is a researcher focused on the relationship between gut microbiota and obesity."}{"title": "MURPHY R:Murphy R is a researcher who has studied the effects of antibiotics on body mass index in children."}{"title": "DAO MC:Dao MC is a researcher who has investigated the role of Akkermansia muciniphila in metabolic health."}{"title": "THUNY F:Thuny F is a researcher who has studied the link between vancomycin treatment and obesity."}{"title": "TREHAN I:Trehan I is a researcher involved in the management of severe acute malnutrition and its implications for health."}{"title": "AJSLV TA:Ajslev TA is a researcher who has studied the impact of gut microbiota on childhood obesity."}{"title": "ALLIN KH:Allin KH is a researcher focused on the mechanisms of gut microbiota in type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "MEBRERZ M:"}{"title": "GUT MICROBIOTA:Gut microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms living in the digestive tracts of humans and other animals, which play a crucial role in health and disease."}{"title": "PEPTIC ULCER DISEASE:Peptic ulcer disease is a condition where open sores develop on the lining of the stomach or the first part of the small intestine."}{"title": "PEPTIDE YY:Peptide YY is a hormone released by the gut that helps to regulate appetite and energy balance."}{"title": "INULIN-TYPE FRUCTANS:Inulin-type fructans are a type of prebiotic fiber that can promote gut health and influence metabolism."}{"title": "ENDOCANNABINOID SYSTEM:The endocannabinoid system is a complex cell-signaling system that plays a role in regulating various physiological processes, including appetite and metabolism."}{"title": "MEDICI F:Medici F is a researcher who studied the concordance rate for type II diabetes mellitus in monozygotic twins."}{"title": "MORAN CP:Moran CP is a researcher focusing on the role of gut microbiota in obesity and its potential as a therapeutic target."}{"title": "TILG H:Tilg H is a researcher who has explored the interactions between obesity, metabolic syndrome, and microbiota."}{"title": "PICKUP JC:Pickup JC is a researcher who has investigated the relationship between type II diabetes mellitus and the innate immune system."}{"title": "FREELAND KR:Freeland KR is a researcher who studied the adaptation of colonic fermentation and its effects on glucagon-like peptide-1 secretion."}{"title": "MUCCIOLO GG:Muccioli GG is a researcher who studied the endocannabinoid system's link to gut microbiota and adipogenesis."}{"title": "BURCELIN R:Burcelin R is a researcher who has investigated the interactions between the immune system and microbiota in the context of metabolic diseases. His work focuses on understanding the cross-talk between these two systems and how it influences metabolic health."}{"title": "ANDERSSON AF:"}{"title": "MUCCIOLI GG:Muccioli GG is a researcher who contributed to the study linking the endocannabinoid system to gut microbiota and adipogenesis."}{"title": "NASLAIN D:Naslain D is a researcher involved in the study of the immuno-microbiota cross-talk in metabolic diseases."}{"title": "REIGSTAD CS:Reigstad CS is a researcher who co-authored studies on gut microbiota and its effects on metabolism."}{"title": "LAMBERT DM:Lambert DM is a researcher who contributed to the study of the endocannabinoid system and gut microbiota."}{"title": "DELZENNE NM:Delzenne NM is a researcher focused on the relationship between gut microbiota and metabolic diseases."}{"title": "GARIDOU L:Garidou L is a researcher involved in the study of the microbiota's role in metabolic diseases."}{"title": "POMI\u00c9 C:Pomi\u00e9 C is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of immuno-microbiota interactions."}{"title": "MUSSO G:Musso G is a researcher focused on exploring the connections between obesity, diabetes, and gut microbiota. Through their studies, Musso G has contributed to the understanding of how these factors interact and influence each other, highlighting the significance of gut microbiota in the context of metabolic diseases such as obesity and diabetes."}{"title": "GAMBINO R:Gambino R is a researcher dedicated to studying the effects of gut microbiota on metabolic health. Through their investigations, Gambino R has contributed to the understanding of how gut microbiota influences various aspects of metabolic health."}{"title": "CASSADER M:Cassader M is a researcher dedicated to exploring the relationship between gut microbiota and obesity. Through their investigations, Cassader M has contributed to the understanding of how gut microbiota influences obesity, highlighting the significance of this area of study in the field of health and nutrition."}{"title": "YADAV H:Yadav H is a researcher who studied the beneficial metabolic effects of probiotics on GLP-1 hormone secretion."}{"title": "LEE J-H:Lee J-H is a researcher involved in the study of probiotics and their metabolic effects."}{"title": "LLOYD J:Lloyd J is a researcher who contributed to the study of probiotics and GLP-1 hormone secretion."}{"title": "WALTER P:Walter P is a researcher who has studied the effects of probiotics on metabolism."}{"title": "RANE SG:Rane SG is a researcher who has investigated the metabolic effects of probiotics."}{"title": "BINDLES LB:Bindels LB is a researcher focused on the physiological relevance of GPR43/FFA2 in metabolism."}{"title": "DEWULF EM:Dewulf EM is a researcher studying the therapeutic prospects of GPR43/FFA2."}{"title": "KUWAHARA A:Kuwahara A is a researcher who has studied the contributions of colonic short-chain fatty acid receptors in energy homeostasis."}{"title": "EVERARD A:Everard A is a researcher who has explored the relationship between gut microbiota and GLP-1."}{"title": "VELASQUEZ-MANOFF M:Velasquez-Manoff M is a researcher who has written about the gut microbiome and its implications."}{"title": "DUNCAN SH:Duncan SH is a researcher who has focused on the human colonic microbiota in relation to diet, obesity, and weight loss. His studies have explored how these factors interact and influence each other, contributing to a deeper understanding of the microbiota's role in human health."}{"title": "LOBLEY GE:Lobley GE is a researcher involved in the study of gut microbiota and obesity."}{"title": "HOLTROP G:Holtrop G is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of gut microbiota in relation to diet and obesity."}{"title": "INCE J:Ince J is a researcher studying the relationship between gut microbiota and weight loss."}{"title": "JOHNSTONE AM:Johnstone AM is a researcher who has investigated the role of gut microbiota in obesity."}{"title": "LOUIS P:Louis P is a researcher focused on the human colonic microbiota and its association with diet."}{"title": "HOLD GL:Hold GL is a researcher focused on the role of gut microbiota in inflammatory bowel disease. They have conducted studies exploring how gut microbiota contributes to the pathogenesis of this condition, aiming to deepen the understanding of its implications in inflammatory bowel disease."}{"title": "SMITH M:Smith M is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of gut microbiota in inflammatory bowel disease."}{"title": "GRANGE C:Grange C is a researcher studying the role of gut microbiota in disease pathogenesis."}{"title": "WATT ER:Watt ER is a researcher involved in the study of gut microbiota and its implications for health."}{"title": "EL-OMAR EM:El-Omar EM is a researcher focused on the role of gut microbiota in inflammatory bowel disease."}{"title": "MUKHOPADHYA I:Mukhopadhya I is a researcher studying the gut microbiota's role in disease."}{"title": "TURNBAUGH P:Turnbaugh P is a researcher who has studied the effect of diet on the human gut microbiome."}{"title": "RIDAURA V:Ridaura V is a researcher involved in the metagenomic analysis of the human gut microbiome."}{"title": "FAITH J:Faith J is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of the human gut microbiome."}{"title": "REY F:Rey F is a researcher studying the effects of diet on gut microbiota."}{"title": "GORDON J:Gordon J is a researcher focused on the relationship between diet and the human gut microbiome."}{"title": "ZHANG H:Zhang H is a researcher and co-author known for contributions to the field of surgery and obesity research. They co-authored a study published in the International Journal of Surgery, which examined the effect of early oral feeding on the short-term outcomes of patients undergoing laparoscopic distal gastrectomy. Additionally, Zhang H has conducted research on the human gut microbiota, focusing on its role in obesity and the changes that occur following gastric bypass surgery."}{"title": "DIBAISE JK:DiBaise JK is a researcher involved in the study of gut microbiota and obesity."}{"title": "ZUCCOLO A:Zuccolo A is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of gut microbiota in obesity."}{"title": "KUDRNA D:Kudrna D is a researcher studying the effects of gut microbiota on health."}{"title": "BRAIDOTTI M:Braidotti M is a researcher involved in the study of gut microbiota and obesity."}{"title": "YU Y:Yu Y is a researcher who has studied the relationship between gut microbiota and obesity."}{"title": "PARAMESWARAN P:Parameswaran P is a researcher focused on the human gut microbiota and its implications."}{"title": "CROWELL MD:Crowell MD is a researcher studying the effects of gut microbiota on health."}{"title": "WING R:Wing R is a researcher who has investigated the relationship between gut microbiota and obesity."}{"title": "RITTMANN BE:Rittmann BE is a researcher involved in the study of gut microbiota and its effects."}{"title": "KRAJMALNIK-BROWN R:Krajmalnik-Brown R is a researcher studying the human gut microbiota in obesity."}{"title": "LEY RE:Ley RE is a researcher who has investigated the relationship between obesity and the human microbiome."}{"title": "KNIGHT RD:Knight RD is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of human gut microbes associated with obesity."}{"title": "SCHWIERTEZ A:Schwiertz A is a researcher who studied the microbiota and short-chain fatty acids in lean and overweight subjects."}{"title": "JUMPERTZ R:Jumpertz R is a researcher who has investigated the associations between gut microbes, caloric load, and nutrient absorption."}{"title": "KALLUS SJ:Kallus SJ is a researcher studying the intestinal microbiota and its relationship with obesity."}{"title": "ARMOUGOM F:Armougom F is a researcher who monitored bacterial communities in the human gut microbiota."}{"title": "HOOPER LV:Hooper LV is a researcher who has analyzed commensal host-microbial relationships in the intestine."}{"title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF OBESITY:The International Journal of Obesity is a scientific journal dedicated to publishing research related to obesity and weight loss. It emphasizes studies that explore the impact of obesity on health, contributing to the understanding of this significant public health issue."}{"title": "WORLD JOURNAL OF GASTROENTEROLOGY:The World Journal of Gastroenterology is a peer-reviewed journal dedicated to advancing research in the field of gastroenterology. It focuses on a wide range of topics related to gastrointestinal diseases and treatments, including the study of gut microbiota and its connection to obesity. The journal also covers research on gastrointestinal health, emphasizing areas such as nutrition support in pancreatitis. By publishing articles on various aspects of gastroenterology, the World Journal of Gastroenterology serves as a vital resource for researchers and healthcare professionals interested in the latest findings and developments in gastrointestinal health and diseases."}{"title": "FRONT MICROBIOLOGY:A journal that publishes research on microbiology, including studies on gut microbiota and its impact on health."}{"title": "CELL HOST MICROBE:A journal that focuses on the interactions between hosts and microbes, including research on gut microbiota and obesity."}{"title": "MICROBIAL CELL FACTORIES:A journal that publishes research on microbial biotechnology, including studies on gut microbiota and health."}{"title": "C57BL/6J MICE:A specific strain of mice commonly used in obesity research to study metabolic adaptations to high-fat diets."}{"title": "BIFIDOBACTERIUM ANIMALIS:A type of bacteria in the gut microbiota that is often studied in relation to obesity and gut health."}{"title": "METHANOBREVIBACTER SMITHII:A type of archaea in the gut microbiota, studied for its association with obesity."}{"title": "INFLAMMATORY BOWEL DISEASE:Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD) refers to a group of inflammatory conditions affecting the colon and small intestine, characterized by chronic inflammation of the gastrointestinal tract. This group primarily includes Crohn's disease and ulcerative colitis. The development and progression of IBD may be influenced by gut microbiota, highlighting the complex interplay between the immune system and the microorganisms residing in the gut."}{"title": "GUT MICROBIOTA COMPOSITION:The specific makeup of microorganisms in the gut, which can affect health outcomes, including obesity."}{"title": "HIGH-FAT DIET:A diet that is high in fat content, often used in research to study its effects on obesity and gut microbiota."}{"title": "HUMAN GUT MICROBIOTA:"}{"title": "HOSPITAL VIRGEN DE LA SALUD:Hospital Virgen de la Salud is a healthcare institution situated in Toledo, Spain. It specializes in endocrinology and nutrition, providing comprehensive medical services in these fields."}{"title": "FUNDACI\u00d3N JIM\u00c9NEZ D\u00cdAZ:Fundaci\u00f3n Jim\u00e9nez D\u00edaz is a healthcare foundation located in Madrid, Spain. It is recognized for providing a range of medical services and education to the community. The foundation is particularly noted for its expertise in endocrinology and nutrition, making it a significant institution in these fields. Through its comprehensive healthcare offerings, Fundaci\u00f3n Jim\u00e9nez D\u00edaz plays a vital role in promoting health and wellness in the region."}{"title": "CLOTILDE V\u00c1ZQUEZ:Clotilde V\u00e1zquez is the head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Fundaci\u00f3n Jim\u00e9nez D\u00edaz in Madrid."}{"title": "B\u00c1RBARA C\u00c1NOVAS:B\u00e1rbara C\u00e1novas is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital Virgen de la Salud in Toledo."}{"title": "VIRGINIA PE\u00d1A:Virginia Pe\u00f1a is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital Virgen de la Salud in Toledo."}{"title": "OFELIA LLAMAZARES:Ofelia Llamazares is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital Virgen de la Salud in Toledo."}{"title": "MIRIAM P\u00c9REZ-PELAYO:Miriam P\u00e9rez-Pelayo is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition. In addition to her clinical expertise, she is also an author who has contributed to the chapter on the importance of diet in the management of diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "VICTORIA ALC\u00c1ZAR:Victoria Alc\u00e1zar is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition. In addition to her clinical expertise, she is also an author who has contributed to the chapter on the importance of diet in the management of diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "PURIFICACI\u00d3N MART\u00cdNEZ DE ICAYA:Purificaci\u00f3n Mart\u00ednez de Icaya is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition. In addition to her clinical expertise, she is also an author who has contributed to the chapter on the importance of diet in the management of diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "YAIZA GARC\u00cdA DELGADO:Yaiza Garc\u00eda Delgado is a healthcare professional specializing in nutritional assessment and dietary management within the field of oncology. She contributes to nutritional support for patients undergoing cancer treatment, focusing on optimizing their dietary needs to enhance overall health and well-being."}{"title": "MAR\u00cdA DEL PINO ALBERICHE RUANO:Mar\u00eda del Pino Alberiche Ruano is a medical professional specializing in nutrition and dietary management."}{"title": "ROSA MAR\u00cdA S\u00c1NCHEZ HERN\u00c1NDEZ:Rosa Mar\u00eda S\u00e1nchez Hern\u00e1ndez is a medical professional specializing in nutrition and dietary management."}{"title": "RA\u00daL ALBERTO GONZ\u00c1LEZ MEDINA:Ra\u00fal Alberto Gonz\u00e1lez Medina is a medical professional specializing in nutrition and dietary management."}{"title": "HEALTHCARE COSTS:Healthcare costs associated with diabetes management can be significantly reduced through proper nutritional treatment."}{"title": "HEALTHY DIET:A healthy diet is crucial for managing diabetes, as it focuses on balanced nutrition to maintain stable blood sugar levels. It is essential for diabetic patients to achieve glycemic control and promote overall health. A healthy diet encompasses a variety of foods that provide necessary nutrients, helping to maintain or improve overall health."}{"title": "COSTS HOSPITALARIOS:Hospital costs refer to the expenses incurred for medical care, which can be reduced through effective dietary management in diabetes."}{"title": "DIABETIC PATIENT:"}{"title": "DIETAS POR RACIONES:Dietas por raciones refers to dietary plans that focus on the exchange units or portions of food groups, allowing flexibility in food choices and meal planning."}{"title": "UNIDADES DE INTERCAMBIO:Unidades de intercambio are units used in dietary planning to help manage carbohydrate intake, particularly for individuals with diabetes."}{"title": "CEREALES:Cereales, or cereals, are grains that serve as a staple in many diets around the world, providing essential carbohydrates and nutrients. They are often combined with legumes to enhance the protein quality in diets. Cereales are particularly important in a child's diet, as they offer vital nutrients necessary for growth and development. \n\nHowever, the purine content in different types of cereales can vary, with some having low levels that may impact uric acid levels in the body. Additionally, while cereales are generally considered non-dairy foods, they may contain galactose, which necessitates caution for individuals with galactosemia. \n\nCereales are also permitted in modified diets and are recommended during episodes of diarrhea, with options such as rice, wheat, and oats suggested for their nutritional benefits. It is important to note that some cereales can contain gluten, making them unsuitable for individuals with celiac disease. Overall, cereales are a fundamental part of many diets, but specific dietary restrictions must be considered for certain health conditions."}{"title": "TUB\u00c9RCULOS:TUB\u00c9RCULOS, which include root vegetables such as potatoes and sweet potatoes, are gluten-free foods that serve as significant sources of carbohydrates in diets. These tubers are particularly suitable for celiac patients, providing essential nutrients without the presence of gluten."}{"title": "PAUTAS DE INSULINIZACI\u00d3N:Pautas de Insulinizaci\u00f3n are the guidelines for insulin administration that individuals with diabetes must follow to manage their condition effectively."}{"title": "LIPEMIA:Lipemia refers to the presence of excess lipids in the blood, which can be a concern for individuals with diabetes."}{"title": "ESTILO DE VIDA:Estilo de vida refers to lifestyle choices, including diet and physical activity, which are crucial for managing diabetes."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD RENAL DIAB\u00c9TICA:Enfermedad Renal Diab\u00e9tica refers to kidney disease that can occur in individuals with diabetes, necessitating specific dietary considerations."}{"title": "ACIDOS GRASOS MONOINSATURADOS:\u00c1cidos Grasos Monoinsaturados are healthy fats recommended for individuals with diabetes, particularly in the context of the Mediterranean diet."}{"title": "LDL COLESTEROL:LDL Colesterol refers to low-density lipoprotein cholesterol, which is a type of cholesterol that individuals with diabetes need to manage through dietary choices."}{"title": "EASD:The European Association for the Study of Diabetes (EASD) is an organization dedicated to advancing the understanding and management of diabetes. It provides comprehensive guidelines and evidence-based recommendations for diabetes care and research, aiming to improve outcomes for individuals affected by the condition. Through its initiatives, EASD plays a crucial role in shaping best practices in diabetes management."}{"title": "GLYCEMIA:Glycemia refers to the presence of glucose in the blood, a critical factor in managing diabetes. It is essential for individuals with diabetes to carefully monitor their glycemia levels, particularly during pregnancy and lactation, to ensure proper health outcomes for both the mother and the child."}{"title": "HIGH GLYCEMIC INDEX FOODS:High glycemic index foods are those that cause a rapid increase in blood sugar levels and are generally advised to be limited in a diabetic diet."}{"title": "LOW GLYCEMIC INDEX FOODS:Low glycemic index foods are those that result in a slower, more gradual increase in blood sugar levels, recommended for better glycemic control."}{"title": "POLYUNSATURATED FATTY ACIDS:Polyunsaturated fatty acids, such as omega-3s, are beneficial fats that can help reduce the risk of cardiovascular disease, particularly in diabetic patients."}{"title": "EUROPEAN ASSOCIATION FOR STUDY OF DIABETES:"}{"title": "SACAROSA:SACAROSA, also known as sucrose or saccharose, is a disaccharide composed of glucose and fructose. It is a common carbohydrate found in many nutritional products, providing sweetness and energy. While it can be added to some infant formulas, it is important to consume SACAROSA in moderation to prevent potential health issues, particularly in children. \n\nSACAROSA plays a significant role in dietary carbohydrates, but its consumption can lead to the production of fructose, which may affect individuals with fructose malabsorption. Additionally, it is recommended that individuals with diabetes substitute SACAROSA in their diets, as it is often discussed in the context of dietary recommendations for diabetes management. \n\nIn sports nutrition, SACAROSA is included in sports drinks to provide energy and enhance flavor. However, it must be eliminated from the diet of individuals with hereditary fructose intolerance due to the potential adverse effects. Overall, while SACAROSA is a widely used sugar, its consumption should be carefully managed based on individual health needs."}{"title": "EDULCORANTES:Edulcorantes are sweeteners that serve as sugar substitutes in a variety of food products. They are particularly relevant in discussions surrounding dietary recommendations for diabetes management, as they provide an alternative to sugar while helping to control blood sugar levels."}{"title": "J\u00d3VENES:J\u00f3venes refers to young people, who are also considered in dietary recommendations for diabetes management."}{"title": "CALOR\u00cdAS:CALOR\u00cdAS refers to the units of energy that are essential for nutritional needs in patients. It represents the energy content in food, which plays a critical role in managing diabetes through diet. Additionally, calor\u00edas are a measure of energy that the body obtains from food, and their appropriate intake is fundamental for maintaining nutritional status in patients with renal diseases."}{"title": "ALMIDONES:Almidones refers to starches, which are carbohydrates that can impact blood sugar levels and are discussed in dietary guidelines for diabetes."}{"title": "EDULCORANTES CAL\u00d3RICOS:Edulcorantes cal\u00f3ricos refers to caloric sweeteners that are compared to other sweeteners in terms of their effects on diabetes management."}{"title": "EDULCORANTES NO CAL\u00d3RICOS:Edulcorantes no cal\u00f3ricos refers to non-caloric sweeteners that are discussed in the context of diabetes management."}{"title": "ASPARTAMO:Aspartame (E951), commonly referred to as Aspartamo, is a low-calorie artificial sweetener widely utilized in a variety of food products and beverages. It is particularly noted in dietary recommendations for individuals with diabetes, as it provides a sweet taste without the added calories associated with sugar."}{"title": "SUCRALOSA:Sucralosa, also known as sucralose (E955), is a non-caloric sweetener that serves as a chlorinated derivative of sucrose. It is widely utilized in various food products and is particularly relevant in the context of dietary management for diabetes, offering a sweetening option without contributing calories."}{"title": "TAUMATINA:Taumatina is a natural sweetener derived from the katemfe fruit, recognized for its intense sweetness. It is often mentioned in dietary recommendations for diabetes management, highlighting its potential benefits for individuals seeking healthier alternatives to sugar. As a natural sweetener, Taumatina (also known as Thaumatin, E957) serves as a suitable option for those looking to reduce sugar intake while still enjoying sweet flavors."}{"title": "ESTEVIA:Estevia is a natural sweetener that is particularly relevant in the context of dietary management for diabetes. It is derived from the leaves of the Stevia rebaudiana plant and is known by its food additive code E960. Estevia serves as a sugar substitute, providing a sweetening option that can help individuals manage their sugar intake while still enjoying sweet flavors."}{"title": "CICLAMATO:Cyclamate (E952) is a non-nutritive sweetener that is often used in combination with other sweeteners to enhance sweetness."}{"title": "NEOTAME:Neotame (E961) is an artificial sweetener that is chemically similar to aspartame but is much sweeter and used in low-calorie foods."}{"title": "ACESULFAMO DE POTASIO:"}{"title": "CANADIAN DIABETES ASSOCIATION:The Canadian Diabetes Association is an organization that focuses on diabetes education, research, and advocacy in Canada."}{"title": "LOCKWOOD D:Lockwood D is an author who contributed to the literature on diabetes management and education."}{"title": "FREY ML:Frey ML is an author who contributed to the literature on diabetes management and education."}{"title": "GLANDISH NA:Glandish NA is an author who contributed to the literature on diabetes management and education."}{"title": "HISS RG:Hiss RG is an author who contributed to the literature on diabetes management and education."}{"title": "BERGENTAL RM:Bergenstal RM is an author who contributed to the management guidelines for diabetes care."}{"title": "BUSE JB:Buse JB is an author who contributed to the management guidelines for diabetes care."}{"title": "DIAMANT M:Diamant M is an author who contributed to the management guidelines for diabetes care."}{"title": "NAUCK M:Nauck M is an author who contributed to the management guidelines for diabetes care."}{"title": "DWORATZEK PD:Dworatzek PD is an author who contributed to the literature on nutrition therapy for diabetes."}{"title": "SANTIAGO J:Santiago J is an author who contributed to the literature on diabetes management."}{"title": "TOUMILHETO J:Toumilheto J is an author who contributed to the Finnish diabetes prevention study."}{"title": "KNOWLER WC:Knowler WC is an author who contributed to the Diabetes Prevention Program research."}{"title": "CHROMIUM:Chromium is a trace mineral that has garnered attention for its potential role in enhancing insulin sensitivity, particularly in individuals with diabetes. It is recognized as an essential nutrient, with recommended daily intake levels specified in dietary guidelines. This mineral, often referred to as \"Cromo,\" plays a significant role in metabolic processes and is important for overall health."}{"title": "COULSTON AM:Coulston AM is an author of a technical review on nutrition principles for managing diabetes and related complications."}{"title": "UK PROSPECTIVE DIABETES STUDY:The UK Prospective Diabetes Study is a research group that studied the response of fasting plasma glucose to diet therapy in type II diabetic patients."}{"title": "GOLDSTEIN DJ:Goldstein DJ is an author who discussed the beneficial health effects of modest weight loss."}{"title": "POUND LOST TRIAL:The POUND Lost Trial is a study that examined the effects of different weight-loss diets on various health metrics."}{"title": "DIRECT GROUP:The DIRECT Group is a research group that conducted a randomized controlled trial on weight loss with different diet types."}{"title": "WHEELER ML:Wheeler ML is an author who conducted a systematic review of macronutrients, food groups, and eating patterns in diabetes management."}{"title": "GANNON MC:Gannon MC is an author who researched the effects of a high-protein, low-carbohydrate diet on blood glucose control in type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "PAN Y:Pan Y is an author who conducted a meta-analysis on low protein diets for diabetic nephropathy."}{"title": "RODRIGUEZ-VILLAR C:Rodriguez-Villar C is an author who contributed to research on dietary interventions in diabetes management."}{"title": "LEAN MEJ:"}{"title": "DAFNE STUDY GROUP:The DAFNE Study Group focuses on training in flexible, intensive insulin management for people with type 1 diabetes."}{"title": "NUTRITION RECOMMENDATIONS:Nutrition recommendations are guidelines provided for managing diabetes through dietary choices."}{"title": "FRANZ MJ:Franz MJ is a prominent researcher and co-author of the American Diabetes Association's nutrition therapy recommendations for diabetes management. He is recognized for his expertise in evidence-based nutrition principles and has made significant contributions to the field of diabetes treatment and prevention."}{"title": "RODR\u00cdGUEZ-VILLAR C:Rodr\u00edguez-Villar C is a researcher who studied the effects of a high monounsaturated fat, olive oil-rich diet on patients with type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "CROCHEMORE ICC:Crochemore ICC is a researcher who investigated the effects of omega-3 polyunsaturated fatty acid supplementation on women with type 2 diabetes and obesity."}{"title": "KROMHOUT D:Kromhout D is a researcher known for his significant contributions to the field of nutrition and cardiovascular health. He is involved in the Seven Countries Study, which investigates the impact of dietary fats on heart disease mortality. Additionally, Kromhout D has conducted research examining the relationship between n-3 fatty acids and cardiovascular events specifically in post-myocardial infarction patients who have diabetes. His work highlights the importance of dietary components in managing heart health and preventing cardiovascular diseases."}{"title": "BOSCH J:Bosch J is a researcher involved in the Origin Trial, which examined n-3 fatty acids and cardiovascular outcomes in patients with dysglycemia."}{"title": "KRIS-ETHERTON PM:Kris-Etherton PM is a prominent researcher and author known for his extensive studies on the impact of fish consumption and omega-3 fatty acids on cardiovascular disease. His research also delves into the effects of individual fatty acids on plasma lipids and lipoproteins, contributing valuable insights to the understanding of dietary influences on heart health."}{"title": "DELHANTY LM:Delahanty LM is a researcher who contributed to the Diabetes Control and Complications Trial, focusing on diet and glycated hemoglobin in type 1 diabetes."}{"title": "BRAND-MILLER J:Brand-Miller J is a researcher who conducted a meta-analysis on low-glycemic index diets in diabetes management."}{"title": "OPPERMAN AM:Opperman AM is a researcher who analyzed the health effects of using the glycemic index in meal planning for diabetes."}{"title": "WORAICH ML:Woraich ML is a researcher who studied the effects of high sucrose or aspartame diets on children's behavior and cognitive performance."}{"title": "SERRA-MAJEM L:Serra-Majem L is a researcher who contributed to the Chinch\u00f3n Declaration on low- and no-calorie sweeteners."}{"title": "HOWARD AA:Howard AA is a researcher who conducted a systematic review on the effects of alcohol consumption on diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "GARG A:"}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO SEVERO OCHOA:Hospital Universitario Severo Ochoa is a medical institution located in Legan\u00e9s, Madrid, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "DOLRES DEL OLMO:Dolores del Olmo is an author contributing to the chapter on the importance of diet in diabetes mellitus management."}{"title": "DIETARY APPROACHES TO STOP HYPERTENSION (DASH):The DASH diet is a dietary plan aimed at reducing blood pressure and improving overall health, which may be relevant for individuals with diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "DIETOTHERAPY:Dietotherapy is the use of diet to treat or manage health conditions, particularly relevant for individuals with diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "LACTATION:Lactation is the period after childbirth during which a mother produces milk, and it is recommended for women with diabetes as it can help lower blood sugar levels."}{"title": "VEGETARIAN DIETS:Vegetarian diets, when well-planned, can be suitable for individuals with diabetes, offering health benefits such as lower saturated fat intake."}{"title": "CALORIES:CALORIES refer to a measure of energy provided by food and nutritional products, which is essential for individuals requiring additional energy intake. Managing caloric intake is particularly crucial for individuals with diabetes, as it plays a significant role in their health management across different life stages, including pregnancy and old age. Additionally, CALORIES are the focus of a multicentre, randomised controlled trial that compares the clinical effectiveness and cost-effectiveness of early nutritional support delivered via the parenteral route versus the enteral route in critically ill patients. This trial aims to enhance understanding of how caloric support can be optimized in critical care settings."}{"title": "RAMAD\u00c1N:Ramad\u00e1n is a holy month in the Islamic calendar during which Muslims fast from dawn until sunset, impacting dietary habits and glucose management for those with diabetes."}{"title": "COLEGIO AMERICANO DE MEDICINA DEL DEPORTE:The American College of Sports Medicine is an organization that provides guidelines and recommendations for sports medicine and nutrition."}{"title": "ASOCIACIONES AMERICANA Y CANADIENSE DE DIET\u00c9TICA:The American and Canadian Dietetic Associations are professional organizations that provide dietary guidelines and recommendations for nutrition."}{"title": "SEHRI:Sehri is a pre-dawn meal consumed by Muslims during Ramadan to prepare for the day's fast."}{"title": "IFTARI:Iftari is the meal that breaks the fast at sunset during Ramadan, often rich in sweets and balanced foods."}{"title": "KARELA:Karela is a mixture of vegetables and garlic used by some traditional healers, believed to have hypoglycemic effects."}{"title": "PERSONAS VEGETARIANAS:Vegetarians are individuals who do not consume meat and may require specific dietary considerations for health management."}{"title": "PRODUCTOS ENRIQUECIDOS:Enriched products are foods that have been fortified with additional nutrients, such as vitamin B12 and vitamin D, to support health."}{"title": "COMIT\u00c9 OL\u00cdMPICO INTERNACIONAL:The Comit\u00e9 Ol\u00edmpico Internacional (COI) is an organization that plays a crucial role in the realm of sports nutrition and performance. It is responsible for setting protein intake guidelines specifically tailored for athletes involved in both strength and endurance sports. In addition to these protein intake recommendations, the COI provides comprehensive guidelines and consensus statements that address various aspects of sports nutrition, ensuring that athletes have access to the necessary information to optimize their performance."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTOS DE AMINO\u00c1CIDOS Y PROTE\u00cdNAS:Suplementos de amino\u00e1cidos y prote\u00ednas are products that athletes may use to enhance performance, but the necessity of such supplements is questioned by the Comit\u00e9 Ol\u00edmpico Internacional."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS ERGOG\u00c9NICOS:Alimentos ergog\u00e9nicos are substances that are believed to improve physical performance without being toxic, though their effectiveness is not clearly demonstrated."}{"title": "CAFE\u00cdNA:Cafe\u00edna is a medication and a naturally occurring alkaloid that has notable effects on the central nervous system. It can decrease the stimulating effect on this system, which may seem counterintuitive given its common use as a stimulant. Additionally, Cafe\u00edna is recognized for its potential to reduce the incidence of hypoglycemia during and after exercise when consumed prior to physical activity. This makes it a popular choice among athletes, as it is often used to enhance performance and endurance in various physical activities. Overall, Cafe\u00edna serves as an ergogenic aid, improving athletic performance and physical capacity."}{"title": "CARBOHIDRATOS:Carbohidratos, or carbohydrates, are essential nutrients that play a crucial role in providing energy for the human body. They are organic compounds predominantly found in cereals and are considered a major energy source in the human diet. Carbohidratos are classified as macronutrients that are easily absorbed in the small intestine, particularly within the first 100 centimeters. Their intake is especially important for individuals with diabetes, as it is critical for managing energy levels, particularly during exercise."}{"title": "EHH:EHH, or hyperglycemic hyperosmolar non-ketotic state, is a severe complication of diabetes. It is characterized by extremely high blood sugar levels without the presence of ketones, and it is often observed in elderly patients."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTOS DE HIDRATOS DE CARBONO:Carbohydrate supplements are used to provide quick energy and prevent hypoglycemia during physical activities for individuals with diabetes."}{"title": "MONITORIZACI\u00d3N GLUC\u00c9MICA:Glycemic monitoring is essential for individuals with diabetes to track blood sugar levels and prevent complications such as hypoglycemia."}{"title": "CARBOHIDRATOS DE ABSORCI\u00d3N LENTA:Slow-absorbing carbohydrates are recommended for individuals with diabetes to help maintain stable blood sugar levels and prevent hypoglycemia."}{"title": "NICE-SUGAR STUDY:The NICE-SUGAR study investigated the effects of intensive glucose control in critically ill patients, revealing increased mortality rates with strict control."}{"title": "HYPERGLYCEMIA CONTROL:Hyperglycemia control involves the management of blood glucose levels in both critically ill patients and diabetic individuals to prevent adverse outcomes and complications. This process is crucial for maintaining optimal health and reducing the risk of serious health issues associated with elevated blood sugar levels. By effectively regulating blood glucose, healthcare providers aim to improve patient outcomes and enhance overall well-being."}{"title": "MULTIVITAMINS:Multivitamins are dietary supplements that may be recommended for patients with diabetes to ensure adequate nutrient intake."}{"title": "ISOTONIC SOLUTIONS:Isotonic solutions are used for rehydration in patients experiencing dehydration, particularly in those with diabetes."}{"title": "DIET BASAL:Diet basal refers to a basic dietary plan that may be implemented for patients recovering from acute conditions, including diabetes management."}{"title": "ELECTROLYTE REPLACEMENT:Electrolyte replacement is crucial for patients with diabetes, especially during episodes of dehydration or illness."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS RICAS EN GRASA:Fat-rich formulas designed for patients with diabetes to improve metabolic control and manage postprandial glucose levels."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS DE NE EST\u00c1NDAR:Standard enteral nutrition formulas that are compared with fat-rich formulas in studies involving diabetic patients."}{"title": "GLUCEMIA POSTPRANDIAL:Postprandial glucose refers to blood sugar levels after eating, which are critical to monitor in diabetes management."}{"title": "PACIENTES CON DM:Patients with diabetes mellitus who require specific dietary management to control their blood sugar levels."}{"title": "NECESIDADES DE INSULINA:Insulin needs refer to the amount of insulin required by diabetic patients, which can be influenced by dietary changes."}{"title": "COMPOSICI\u00d3N DE LAS F\u00d3RMULAS:The composition of nutritional formulas is crucial for managing diabetes, particularly in terms of carbohydrate and fat content."}{"title": "GLUCEMIAS BASAL:Basal glucose levels are the baseline blood sugar levels that need to be monitored in diabetic patients."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL SOCIETIES:Nutritional societies provide guidelines and recommendations for dietary management in various health conditions, including diabetes."}{"title": "MUFA:Monounsaturated fatty acids (MUFA) are a type of healthy fat that may influence blood sugar levels and overall health in diabetic patients."}{"title": "PATIENTS WITH DM:Patients with Diabetes Mellitus often require tailored dietary plans to manage their condition effectively."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL MONITORING:Nutritional monitoring involves tracking dietary intake and its effects on health, particularly important for managing diabetes."}{"title": "CALORIC INTAKE:Caloric intake refers to the total number of calories consumed, which is essential for maintaining energy balance in patients, particularly those with increased metabolic demands. It plays a significant role in managing diabetes and preventing complications associated with the condition. Proper management of caloric intake is vital for overall health and well-being."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL FORMULAS RICH IN FAT:Nutritional formulas rich in fat are specialized dietary products designed to help manage blood sugar levels in patients with diabetes."}{"title": "GESTATIONAL DIABETES MELLITUS:Gestational Diabetes Mellitus is a form of diabetes that occurs during pregnancy and requires specific dietary management to ensure the health of both the mother and the baby."}{"title": "NUTRITION THERAPY:Nutrition therapy encompasses dietary interventions designed to address the specific nutritional needs of individuals facing various health challenges. It plays a crucial role in managing diabetes by focusing on dietary strategies that aim to improve health outcomes for those affected by the condition. Additionally, nutrition therapy is also vital for cancer patients, particularly those undergoing treatment for esophageal cancer, as it helps manage their unique nutritional requirements during a critical time in their health journey. Overall, nutrition therapy serves as an essential component in the holistic management of both diabetes and cancer, promoting better health and well-being for affected individuals."}{"title": "MATERNA AND NEWBORN OUTCOMES:Maternal and newborn outcomes refer to the health results for mothers and their babies, particularly in the context of managing gestational diabetes."}{"title": "DIETARY INTERVENTION:Dietary intervention refers to the changes made in a person's diet to manage health conditions, such as gestational diabetes."}{"title": "RANDOMIZED CONTROLLED TRIALS:Randomized controlled trials (RCTs) are studies designed to randomly assign participants to various interventions in order to compare the outcomes of those interventions. These trials are commonly utilized in clinical research, particularly in the fields of nutrition and health, to assess the effects of different treatments or interventions on health outcomes. By employing randomization, RCTs aim to eliminate bias and ensure that the results are attributable to the interventions being tested, thereby providing robust evidence for their efficacy."}{"title": "BOUCHER JL:Boucher JL is a co-author of the American Diabetes Association's nutrition therapy recommendations for diabetes management."}{"title": "CYPRESS M:Cypress M is a contributor to the American Diabetes Association's guidelines on nutrition therapy for diabetes."}{"title": "DUNBAR SA:Dunbar SA is one of the authors involved in the American Diabetes Association's recommendations for diabetes management."}{"title": "MAYER-DAVIS EJ:Mayer-Davis EJ is a contributor to the American Diabetes Association's guidelines on nutrition therapy for diabetes."}{"title": "MOROENO-CASTILLA C:Moreno-Castilla C is an author discussing the role of medical nutrition therapy in managing gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "MAURICIO D:Mauricio D is a co-author of research on medical nutrition therapy for gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "HERN\u00c1NDEZ M:Hern\u00e1ndez M is involved in the research regarding medical nutrition therapy for gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "METZGER BE:Metzger BE is a prominent researcher recognized for his significant contributions to the field of gestational diabetes mellitus. He is a key author of the summary and recommendations from the Fifth International Workshop-Conference on Gestational Diabetes Mellitus. Additionally, Metzger BE played a vital role in the development of the International Association of Diabetes and Pregnancy Study Groups recommendations, specifically focusing on the diagnosis and classification of hyperglycemia in pregnancy. His work has been influential in shaping guidelines and practices related to diabetes management during pregnancy."}{"title": "BUCHANAN TA:Buchanan TA is a contributor to the recommendations for managing gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "COUSTAN DR:Coustan DR is one of the authors of the guidelines for managing gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "DE LEIVA A:De Leiva A is a contributor to the recommendations for managing gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "DUNGER DB:Dunger DB is involved in the recommendations for managing gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "HADDEN DR:Hadden DR is a co-author of the guidelines for managing gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "HAN S:Han S is a researcher who has reviewed dietary advice for women with gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "CROWTHER CA:Crowther CA is a co-author of a systematic review on dietary advice for gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "MIDDLETON P:Middleton P is involved in the systematic review of dietary advice for women with gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "HEATLEY E:Heatley E is a contributor to the systematic review on dietary advice for gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "VIANA LV:Viana LV is a researcher who conducted a systematic review on dietary intervention in gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "GROSS JL:Gross JL is a co-author of the systematic review on dietary intervention in gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "AZEVEDO MJ:Azevedo MJ is involved in the systematic review of dietary intervention for gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "SCHOENAKER DA:Schoenaker DA is a researcher who reviewed the role of dietary patterns in the development of gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "MISHRA GD:Mishra GD is a co-author of the systematic review on dietary patterns and gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "CALLAWAY LK:Callaway LK is involved in the research on dietary patterns related to gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "SOEDAMAH-MUTHU SS:Soedamah-Muthu SS is a contributor to the systematic review on dietary patterns and gestational diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "HELLER SR:Heller SR is a co-author of the review on treating type 2 diabetes in older adults."}{"title": "MILLER MA:Miller MA is involved in the review of type 2 diabetes treatment in older adults."}{"title": "G\u00d3MEZ HUELGAS R:G\u00f3mez Huelgas R is a contributor to the consensus conference on treating type 2 diabetes in older patients."}{"title": "D\u00cdEZ ESPINO J:D\u00edez Espino J is involved in the consensus conference on diabetes treatment in older adults."}{"title": "FORMIGA F:Formiga F is a co-author of the consensus conference on treating type 2 diabetes in older patients."}{"title": "LAFITA TEJEDOR J:Lafita Tejedor J is a contributor to the consensus conference on diabetes treatment in older adults."}{"title": "RODR\u00cdGUEZ MA\u00d1AS L:Rodr\u00edguez Ma\u00f1as L is involved in the consensus conference on treating type 2 diabetes in older patients."}{"title": "GONZ\u00c1LEZ SARMIENTO E:Gonz\u00e1lez Sarmiento E is a contributor to the consensus conference on diabetes treatment in older adults."}{"title": "QURESHI B:Qureshi B is a researcher who has written about diabetes management during Ramadan."}{"title": "AMERICAN COLLEGE OF SPORTS MEDICINE:The American College of Sports Medicine is a professional organization dedicated to the fields of sports medicine and exercise science. It plays a crucial role in providing guidelines and position statements that emphasize the importance of exercise and health, particularly concerning diabetes. Additionally, the organization offers specific recommendations on physical activity and nutrition tailored for individuals with diabetes, aiming to enhance their overall health and well-being."}{"title": "COCHRANE DATABASE SYSTEMATIC REVIEW:The Cochrane Database Systematic Review publishes systematic reviews on health interventions, including those for diabetes management."}{"title": "EVERT AB:"}{"title": "HYPERGLYCEMIC CRISES:Hyperglycemic crises are severe complications of diabetes characterized by extremely high blood sugar levels, requiring immediate medical attention."}{"title": "STEPHENSON EJ:Stephenson EJ is an author who has researched the relationship between exercise, nutrition, and type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "RODRIGUEZ NR:Rodriguez NR is an author involved in the position statement regarding nutrition and athletic performance in relation to diabetes."}{"title": "HORTON WB:Horton WB is an author who has reviewed the care of athletes with type 1 diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "IB\u00c1\u00d1EZ J.:Ib\u00e1\u00f1ez J. is an author who contributed to the guide on nutrition and sports for diabetes management."}{"title": "GARGALLO-FERN\u00c1NDEZ M.:Gargallo-Fern\u00e1ndez M. is an author who has provided clinical recommendations for sports practice in patients with diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "MEZQUITA-RAYA P.:Mezquita-Raya P. is an author who has worked on the evaluation and management of hypoglycemia in diabetes patients."}{"title": "P\u00c9REZ P\u00c9REZ A.:P\u00e9rez P\u00e9rez A. is an author who has written about diet in diabetes management."}{"title": "SENIOR AURELIAN OFFICIALS:Senior Aurelian officials are government representatives involved in the negotiations and management of diabetes-related health policies."}{"title": "QURESHI B.:"}{"title": "ANNA BONADA:Anna Bonada is an author who has contributed to the field of nutrition and dietetics, particularly in clinical nutrition."}{"title": "ROSER TRALLERO:Roser Trallero is an author involved in research and publications related to nutrition and dietetics."}{"title": "M. ENG\u00c0RCIA SAL\u00d3:M. Engr\u00e0cia Sal\u00f3 is an author who has contributed to the literature on nutrition and dietetics."}{"title": "ED DOYMA:Ed Doyma is a publishing house that has published works on nutrition and dietetics."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO INSULAR DE GRAN CANARIA:The Hospital Universitario Insular de Gran Canaria is a healthcare institution situated in Las Palmas de Gran Canaria. It specializes in endocrinology and nutrition services, and is also involved in research related to these fields. This institution plays a significant role in providing specialized medical care and advancing knowledge in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "SECCI\u00d3N DE ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:The Secci\u00f3n de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n is a department within the Hospital Universitario Insular de Gran Canaria focused on endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "UNIDAD DE HOSPITALIZACI\u00d3N DE MEDICINA INTERNA:The Unidad de Hospitalizaci\u00f3n de Medicina Interna is a unit within the Hospital Universitario Insular de Gran Canaria that specializes in internal medicine."}{"title": "GRUPO AULA M\u00c9DICA:Grupo Aula M\u00e9dica is a prominent organization engaged in medical education and publishing, with a particular emphasis on nutrition and dietetics. The group is known for producing a variety of educational materials aimed at healthcare professionals, which include guidelines and literature in the medical field. They hold copyright for several significant texts, including those focused on clinical nutrition, pediatric nutrition, and clinical nutrition and metabolism. Additionally, Grupo Aula M\u00e9dica is involved in publishing works related to evidence-based medicine and oncology, further contributing to the advancement of medical knowledge and practices. Through their efforts, they aim to enhance the education and resources available to healthcare providers."}{"title": "EVIDENCIAS CL\u00cdNICAS:Evidencias cl\u00ednicas sobre el soporte nutricional en el paciente diab\u00e9tico is a systematic review that provides clinical evidence regarding nutritional support for diabetic patients."}{"title": "GLUCOSE METABOLISM DISORDERS:Glucose metabolism disorders are conditions that are addressed in clinical nutrition literature, particularly in relation to dietary management.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "GLUC\u00d3GENO:GLUC\u00d3GENO is a polysaccharide that serves as a crucial form of energy storage in animals and fungi. It primarily exists in the liver and muscle tissues, where it acts as a reserve of glucose, which is essential for various bodily functions. The metabolism of gluc\u00f3geno is particularly important for muscle activity, influencing physical performance and exercise requirements. Additionally, gluc\u00f3geno can be synthesized from fructose metabolism when necessary, highlighting its role in carbohydrate storage and energy management within the body. Overall, gluc\u00f3geno plays a significant role in maintaining energy levels and supporting physical exertion."}{"title": "GLUCONEOG\u00c9NESIS:GLUCONEOG\u00c9NESIS es un proceso biol\u00f3gico que se refiere a la s\u00edntesis de gluc\u00f3geno a partir de glucosa, que ocurre principalmente en el h\u00edgado y los m\u00fasculos. Este proceso es fundamental para el almacenamiento de energ\u00eda en el cuerpo, permitiendo que la glucosa se convierta en gluc\u00f3geno, que puede ser utilizado posteriormente cuando el organismo necesita energ\u00eda."}{"title": "GLUCOLISIS:La glucogen\u00f3lisis es el proceso de degradaci\u00f3n del gluc\u00f3geno para liberar glucosa cuando es necesario."}{"title": "HEXOKINASA:La hexokinasa es una enzima que fosforila la glucosa para mantenerla dentro de las c\u00e9lulas durante la glucogenog\u00e9nesis."}{"title": "GLUC\u00d3GENO FOSFORILASA:GLUC\u00d3GENO FOSFORILASA is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the process of glycogenolysis, which is the breakdown of glycogen into glucose-1-phosphate. This enzyme catalyzes the conversion of glycogen, facilitating the release of glucose-1-phosphate, an important molecule for energy production in the body."}{"title": "GLUCOSA-6-FOSFATO:GLUCOSA-6-FOSFATO es un metabolito clave en el metabolismo de la glucosa y la galactosa. Se trata de una forma fosforilada de la glucosa que desempe\u00f1a un papel fundamental en la gluc\u00f3lisis y el metabolismo del gluc\u00f3geno. Adem\u00e1s, la glucosa-6-fosfato act\u00faa como un intermediario en el metabolismo de la glucosa y es crucial en el proceso de glucogenog\u00e9nesis."}{"title": "GLUCOSA-1-FOSFATO:GLUCOSA-1-FOSFATO is a glucose molecule that has been phosphorylated at the first carbon, making it an important intermediate in glycogen metabolism. It is formed during the conversion of glucose into glycogen, playing a crucial role in the storage and regulation of energy within the body."}{"title": "URIDIN-DIFOSFATO-GLUCOSA:El uridin-difosfato-glucosa es un intermediario en la s\u00edntesis de gluc\u00f3geno que se forma a partir de glucosa-1-fosfato."}{"title": "ENZIMA RAMIFICANTE:Enzima ramificante is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the synthesis of glycogen by introducing \u03b1-1,6 linkages, which are essential for creating the branched structure of glycogen. This enzyme is responsible for forming the branches in the glycogen structure, facilitating its complex architecture that is vital for energy storage in organisms."}{"title": "GLUC\u00d3GENO SINTASA:Gluc\u00f3geno sintasa is an enzyme responsible for the synthesis of glycogen from glucose, playing a key role in glycogenogenesis."}{"title": "GLUCOSA-6-FOSFATASA:Glucosa-6-fosfatasa is an essential enzyme involved in glucose metabolism. It plays a critical role in converting glucose-6-phosphate into glucose, facilitating the release of free glucose into the bloodstream. This enzymatic activity is vital for maintaining normal blood glucose levels. A deficiency in glucosa-6-fosfatasa is central to the diagnosis of glucogenosis de tipo I, also known as enfermedad de Von Gierke, a genetic disorder characterized by impaired glucose production and storage."}{"title": "GLUC\u00d3GENO STORAGE DISEASE:Glycogen Storage Disease (GSD) refers to a group of inherited metabolic disorders that result in abnormal storage of glycogen due to enzyme deficiencies."}{"title": "FOSFORILASA A:Fosforilasa a is the active form of gluc\u00f3geno fosforilasa, responsible for breaking down glycogen into glucose-1-phosphate."}{"title": "FOSFORILASA B:Fosforilasa b is the inactive form of gluc\u00f3geno fosforilasa, which must be activated to participate in glycogen breakdown."}{"title": "UDP-GLUCOSA:UDP-glucosa is a nucleotide sugar that plays a crucial role in metabolism, particularly in the metabolism of galactose. It is essential for the synthesis of glycogen and other macromolecules, functioning as a glucose donor in these biochemical processes."}{"title": "UDP-GLUCOSA PIROFOSFORIILASA:UDP-glucosa pirofosforilasa is an enzyme that catalyzes the formation of UDP-glucose from glucose-1-phosphate and UTP."}{"title": "FOSFOGLUCOMUTASA:Fosfoglucomutasa is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in carbohydrate metabolism by catalyzing the conversion of glucosa-1-fosfato (glucose-1-phosphate) to glucosa-6-fosfato (glucose-6-phosphate). This conversion is essential for facilitating the entry of glucose into various metabolic pathways, thereby contributing to the overall regulation of glucose metabolism."}{"title": "TORRENTE SANGU\u00cdNEO:Torrente sangu\u00edneo refers to the bloodstream, the circulatory system that transports glucose and other nutrients throughout the body."}{"title": "GLUCOGEN\u00d3LISIS:Gluconeogenesis is the metabolic pathway that results in the generation of glucose from non-carbohydrate substrates, primarily occurring in the liver."}{"title": "GLUCOGENOG\u00c9NESIS:Glycogenesis is the process of synthesizing glycogen from glucose, primarily occurring in the liver and muscle tissues."}{"title": "FOSFORILASA KINASA:"}{"title": "GLYCOGEN STORAGE DISEASE TYPE I:Glycogen Storage Disease Type I (GSDI) is a genetic disorder characterized by the accumulation of glycogen in the liver and kidneys due to enzyme deficiencies."}{"title": "HEPATOMEGALY:Hepatomegaly is a clinical condition characterized by the mild enlargement of the liver. It is commonly associated with various metabolic disorders, particularly glycogen storage diseases such as type I glucogenosis (GSDI) and type VI glucogenosis (GSDVI). This condition can also occur in patients with fructose-1,6-bisphosphate deficiency, where fatty acid accumulation contributes to liver enlargement. Additionally, hepatomegaly may be observed in individuals with Wilson's disease, further highlighting its association with a range of hepatic and metabolic disorders. Overall, hepatomegaly serves as an important clinical manifestation indicative of underlying liver-related issues."}{"title": "GLUCOSE-6-PHOSPHATASE:Glucose-6-phosphatase is an enzyme critical for glucose metabolism, deficiency of which leads to GSDI."}{"title": "GLUCOSE-6-PHOSPHATE TRANSPORTER:Glucose-6-phosphate transporter is an enzyme involved in the transport of glucose-6-phosphate within cells, deficiency of which is associated with GSDI."}{"title": "VON GIERKE DISEASE:Von Gierke disease is another name for Glycogen Storage Disease Type I, specifically related to glucose-6-phosphatase deficiency."}{"title": "GLYCOGEN:Glycogen is a multi-branched polysaccharide composed of glucose that functions as a crucial form of energy storage in animals and fungi. It serves as a stored form of glucose within the body, playing a vital role in energy metabolism. In certain conditions, such as Glycogen Storage Disease Type I, glycogen can accumulate excessively, indicating a disruption in normal glycogen metabolism."}{"title": "HEPATOCYTES:Hepatocytes are the main functional cells of the liver, where glucose-6-phosphatase is located and plays a crucial role in glucose metabolism."}{"title": "RENAL TUBULE CELLS:Renal tubule cells are involved in the kidney's function and are affected in Glycogen Storage Disease Type I due to the accumulation of glycogen."}{"title": "ENTEROCYTES:Enterocytes are intestinal cells that also express glucose-6-phosphatase, contributing to glucose metabolism."}{"title": "G6PC:G6PC is a gene associated with glucose-6-phosphatase deficiency, which can lead to various metabolic disorders."}{"title": "SLC37A4:SLC37A4 is a gene that encodes a glucose-6-phosphate transporter, involved in glucose metabolism."}{"title": "GSDIB:Glycogen Storage Disease Type Ib (GSDIb) is a metabolic disorder characterized by the inability to properly metabolize glycogen, leading to various health complications."}{"title": "HEMODIALYSIS:Hemodialysis is a medical procedure utilized to remove waste products and excess fluid from the blood when the kidneys are not functioning properly. It is primarily used to treat patients with kidney failure, including those with chronic kidney disease and severe cases of metabolic disorders. The process involves the filtration of blood through a machine, which effectively cleanses the blood of harmful substances. Additionally, hemodialysis often necessitates specific nutritional considerations for patients, particularly in monitoring phosphorus intake to ensure optimal health outcomes."}{"title": "ADENOMAS HEP\u00c1TICOS:Hepatic adenomas are benign tumors of the liver that can develop in patients with metabolic disorders, particularly during the second to third decade of life. These tumors are notably associated with glycogen storage disease type III (GSDIII), indicating a specific metabolic condition that may contribute to their formation."}{"title": "INFANTILE HYPOGLYCEMIA:Infantile hypoglycemia refers to low blood sugar levels in infants, which can lead to cognitive deterioration if severe and frequent."}{"title": "GOUT:Gout is a form of inflammatory arthritis that is characterized by sudden and severe pain, redness, and tenderness in the joints. This condition often occurs due to hyperuricemia, which is an elevated level of uric acid in the blood, commonly associated with metabolic disorders. Gout can lead to significant discomfort and swelling, making it a painful experience for those affected."}{"title": "COGNITIVE DETERIORATION:Cognitive deterioration can occur in patients with frequent severe hypoglycemia during childhood, affecting their development."}{"title": "KIDNEY FAILURE:Kidney failure is a serious condition that may require hemodialysis or kidney transplant, often seen in patients with metabolic disorders."}{"title": "DISLIPEMIA MIXTA:Mixed dyslipidemia refers to abnormal levels of lipids in the blood, which can increase cardiovascular risk."}{"title": "FENOTIPO PECULIAR:A peculiar phenotype is a distinct physical appearance or set of characteristics that can be associated with specific metabolic disorders."}{"title": "NEFROMEGALIA:Nephromegaly is the enlargement of the kidneys, which can occur due to glycogen accumulation in metabolic disorders."}{"title": "COLLABORATIVE EUROPEAN STUDY ON GLYCOGEN STORAGE DISEASE I:A study group that publishes guidelines for the treatment of Glycogen Storage Disease I, focusing on nutritional objectives and recommendations for patients."}{"title": "GLYCOGEN STORAGE DISEASE I:A metabolic disorder that affects the body's ability to store and use glycogen, requiring specific dietary management to maintain normal blood glucose levels."}{"title": "DIAZOXIDE:A medication used to inhibit endogenous insulin production in patients who cannot maintain adequate blood glucose levels through nutritional treatment."}{"title": "ALMID\u00d3N DE MA\u00cdZ:Almid\u00f3n de ma\u00edz, or corn starch, is a carbohydrate derived from corn that serves multiple purposes in nutrition and cooking. It is commonly utilized in enteral nutrition and dietary plans for various age groups, including infants and adults, to help maintain stable blood glucose levels. In addition to its role as a carbohydrate source in nutritional formulas, corn starch is frequently employed as a thickening agent in culinary applications. It is particularly beneficial in dietary treatments for metabolic disorders, where it aids in managing blood glucose levels effectively. Furthermore, corn starch is recommended as a dietary component for patients, especially before sleep, to support the maintenance of healthy blood glucose levels."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ADECUADA:The provision of appropriate nutrition to ensure proper growth and development in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease I."}{"title": "PERIODOS DE AYUNO:Periods of fasting that patients with Glycogen Storage Disease I must avoid to maintain stable blood glucose levels."}{"title": "ALMID\u00d3N CRUDO DE MA\u00cdZ:Almid\u00f3n crudo de ma\u00edz, or raw corn starch, is a dietary supplement specifically recommended for patients with glycogen storage diseases (GSD), including conditions such as GSDI and GSDIX. It plays a crucial role in managing hypoglycemia by providing a steady release of glucose, which is essential for maintaining normal blood sugar levels. This supplement is particularly beneficial for individuals with McArdle disease, as it helps sustain glucose levels before sleeping, and for those with fructose-1,6-bisphosphate deficiency, aiding in their dietary management and prevention of hypoglycemia. Overall, almid\u00f3n crudo de ma\u00edz is an important dietary component that supports patients in maintaining stable blood glucose levels, especially between meals and during periods of fasting."}{"title": "GSDI:Glycogen Storage Disease I (GSDI) is a metabolic disorder that significantly impairs the body's ability to store and utilize glycogen, resulting in a range of health complications for those affected. This condition exhibits symptoms that are reminiscent of fructose-1,6-bisphosphate deficiency; however, individuals with GSDI maintain normal glycogenolysis. GSDI is characterized by more severe hypoglycemia when compared to Glycogen Storage Disease Type III (GSDIII). Additionally, GSDI has distinct dietary restrictions that differ from those associated with GSDIII, although it shares some similarities in dietary recommendations with this related metabolic disorder. Overall, GSDI presents a unique set of challenges and management strategies for affected individuals."}{"title": "COLLABORATIVE EUROPEAN STUDY:The Collaborative European Study on Glycogen Storage Disease I is a research initiative focused on understanding and providing dietary recommendations for GSDI patients."}{"title": "MAICENA:Maicena is a brand of cornstarch that serves as a dietary treatment for metabolic disorders, particularly in the management of blood glucose levels. It is recognized for its properties as a polysaccharide, which makes it suitable for patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type I (GSDI). Maicena is recommended for these patients due to its slow absorption rate, which helps in maintaining stable blood glucose levels."}{"title": "LACOSTA:Lacosta is a hypothetical individual referenced in dietary recommendations for managing GSDI."}{"title": "SORBITOL:SORBITOL is a sugar alcohol that serves as an artificial sweetener and is commonly used in various food products. It is naturally found in fruits and is known for its high sweetness while containing low calories. Sorbitol is absorbed passively in the intestine; however, it can cause osmotic diarrhea when consumed in large quantities. Additionally, individuals with hereditary fructose intolerance should avoid sorbitol, as it is a product of fructose metabolism. Furthermore, it is recommended that children with Glycogen Storage Disease Type I (GSDI) also avoid sorbitol due to its potential impact on glucose levels."}{"title": "JARABE DE MA\u00cdZ RICO EN FRUCTOSA:\"Jarabe de ma\u00edz rico en fructosa\" is a sweetener derived from corn, commonly utilized in various processed foods and beverages. However, it is important to note that high fructose corn syrup, which is synonymous with jarabe de ma\u00edz rico en fructosa, should be avoided in children with Glycogen Storage Disease Type I (GSDI) due to its potential negative impact on glucose metabolism."}{"title": "LACTOSA:LACTOSA is a disaccharide sugar composed of glucose and galactose, primarily found in milk and dairy products. It plays a significant role in nutrition but can lead to lactose intolerance in some individuals. Lactose intolerance is a condition where the body is unable to properly digest lactose, resulting in various gastrointestinal symptoms. This condition can affect individuals with malabsorption issues, including those with specific gastrointestinal diseases such as Crohn's disease, particularly during flare-ups.\n\nIn addition to its presence in milk, lactose is also found in various packaged foods, where it may be used as a preservative. For individuals with dietary restrictions, such as those with fructose malabsorption or certain metabolic disorders like Glycogen Storage Disease Type I (GSDI), it is important to limit lactose intake. Overall, while lactose is a common component of many foods, its impact on digestion varies among individuals, necessitating careful dietary considerations for those affected by lactose intolerance."}{"title": "GALACTOSA:Galactosa is a monosaccharide that plays a crucial role in the diet of mammals, primarily found in milk and its derivatives. It is a component of lactose and is significant in various metabolic processes. However, galactosa is a simple sugar that can be metabolized in the body, and in certain conditions, it may accumulate, leading to toxicity. This accumulation can pose risks, particularly in individuals with specific metabolic disorders. For instance, when administered, galactosa does not improve hypoglycemia in patients with type I glycogen storage disease (GSDI) and may even exacerbate acidosis. Additionally, it is advised that children with GSDI limit their intake of galactosa. Furthermore, ingestion of galactosa can lead to complications in patients with classic galactosemia, a genetic disorder that impairs the metabolism of this sugar. Overall, while galactosa is an important dietary component, its management is critical in certain medical conditions."}{"title": "DIAREAS TRANSITORIAS:Las diarreas transitorias son efectos secundarios leves que pueden ocurrir al introducir almid\u00f3n de ma\u00edz en la dieta, pero que generalmente se resuelven espont\u00e1neamente."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS MAYORES:Los ni\u00f1os mayores de un a\u00f1o deben consumir al menos tres comidas al d\u00eda con almid\u00f3n de ma\u00edz y snacks frecuentes para mantener niveles de glucosa adecuados."}{"title": "CITRATE:Citrate is a supplement used to alkalinize urine and prevent nephrolithiasis and nephrocalcinosis."}{"title": "BICARBONATE:Bicarbonate is a supplement known for its ability to alkalinize urine, particularly in patients suffering from lactic acidosis. It serves as an alkalizing substance that functions as a buffer in acidic environments. This property makes bicarbonate particularly useful in anaerobic situations, where it helps to neutralize lactic acid and delay the onset of fatigue."}{"title": "NEPHROLITHIASIS:Nephrolithiasis refers to the condition of having kidney stones, which can be influenced by dietary factors. This condition can also be prevented by alkalinizing urine."}{"title": "NEFROCALCINOSIS:Nefrocalcinosis is a condition characterized by calcium deposits in the kidneys, which can be managed with citrate or bicarbonate."}{"title": "GSDIII:Glycogen Storage Disease Type III (GSDIII), also known as Cori disease, is a metabolic disorder characterized by a deficiency of the enzyme amilo-1,6-glucosidase. This deficiency disrupts normal glycogen metabolism, resulting in various complications that primarily affect glucose processing. Individuals with GSDIII may experience muscular and hepatic issues as a result of this disorder. To manage symptoms and complications associated with GSDIII, dietary interventions are recommended, specifically hyperproteic and low carbohydrate diets."}{"title": "AMILO-1,6-GLUCOSIDASA:Amilo-1,6-glucosidasa is an enzyme responsible for glycogen breakdown, and its deficiency leads to GSDIII."}{"title": "GEN AGL:The AGL gene located on chromosome 1p21.2 encodes the enzyme amilo-1,6-glucosidasa, and mutations in this gene are responsible for GSDIII."}{"title": "FIBROSIS HEP\u00c1TICA:Fibrosis hep\u00e1tica is characterized by the formation of excess fibrous connective tissue in the liver, often resulting from chronic liver diseases, such as hereditary hemochromatosis. This condition involves the scarring of liver tissue, which can occur in various patients, including those with Glycogen Storage Disease type III (GSDIII), although it is uncommon for these patients to progress to cirrhosis."}{"title": "HIPERTON\u00cdA:A condition characterized by increased muscle tone, often associated with GSDIII."}{"title": "MIKARDIOPAT\u00cdA HIPERTR\u00d3FICA:Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, a condition affecting the heart muscle, prevalent in GSDIII patients."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL NOCTURNA:NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL NOCTURNA refers to nighttime enteral nutrition, a dietary approach primarily utilized to manage glucose levels in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type III (GSDIII). This method is particularly beneficial for individuals with this condition, as it helps maintain stable glucose levels during the night. However, it is important to note that nocturnal enteral nutrition is generally not necessary for most patients with McArdle disease, as they are able to effectively manage their glucose levels through their dietary intake without the need for additional nighttime nutritional support."}{"title": "HIPOURICEMIA:A condition of elevated uric acid levels in the blood, which can be infrequent in GSDIII patients."}{"title": "AFECTACI\u00d3N RENAL:Renal involvement, a potential complication in patients with GSDIII, though it is also infrequent."}{"title": "GSD0:Glycogen Storage Disease Type 0, a condition characterized by a deficiency in hepatic glycogen synthase, leading to hypoglycemia and other metabolic issues."}{"title": "GLYCOGEN SYNTHASE:An enzyme critical for glycogen synthesis, with its deficiency leading to various glycogen storage diseases."}{"title": "FRUCTOSE:Fructose is a simple sugar, specifically a monosaccharide, that is naturally found in many fruits. It plays a significant role in various metabolic pathways, including energy production. Fructose is permitted in the diets of patients with certain glycogen storage diseases, indicating its potential benefits in specific medical contexts. However, it is also important to note that excessive consumption of fructose can lead to dietary intolerances, highlighting the need for moderation in its intake. Overall, fructose is a versatile sugar with both beneficial and potentially adverse effects depending on the amount consumed."}{"title": "GALACTOSE:Galactose is a monosaccharide sugar that plays a significant role in various metabolic processes. It is a component of lactose, the sugar found in milk, and is also part of galactolipids, which are important for cellular structures. In the context of dietary considerations, galactose is permitted in the diets of patients with certain glycogen storage diseases, indicating its relevance in specific health conditions. Overall, galactose is metabolized by the body and is involved in multiple metabolic pathways, highlighting its importance in human physiology."}{"title": "BIOPSIA HEP\u00c1TICA:BIOPSIA HEP\u00c1TICA, or liver biopsy, is a medical procedure that involves the extraction of a small sample of liver tissue for analysis. This diagnostic procedure is utilized to confirm various liver conditions, including Glycogen Storage Disease Type 0 (GSD0), by studying the liver tissue. Additionally, it plays a crucial role in assessing liver damage due to iron overload in hereditary hemochromatosis and can reveal copper deposits in the liver, which is important for confirming Wilson's disease. Overall, the biopsia hep\u00e1tica is an essential tool in the diagnosis and management of various liver-related health issues."}{"title": "ESTUDIO GEN\u00c9TICO:A genetic study used to confirm the diagnosis of GSD0"}”Ã0␀␀␀␀␀ÇŒ0␀␀␀␀␀œ0␀␀␀␀␀∂–0␀␀␀␀␀ß”0␀␀␀␀␀’0␀␀␀␀␀<’0␀␀␀␀␀>÷0␀␀␀␀␀K◊0␀␀␀␀␀ÿ0␀␀␀␀␀≠ÿ0␀␀␀␀␀{Ÿ0␀␀␀␀␀d⁄0␀␀␀␀␀4€0␀␀␀␀␀V€0␀␀␀␀␀Ô€0␀␀␀␀␀ùﬂ0␀␀␀␀␀P‡0␀␀␀␀␀K·0␀␀␀␀␀œ„0␀␀␀␀␀e‰0␀␀␀␀␀˝‰0␀␀␀␀␀≠Â0␀␀␀␀␀?Ê0␀␀␀␀␀6Ë0␀␀␀␀␀ÅÈ0␀␀␀␀␀&Í0␀␀␀␀␀^Ï0␀␀␀␀␀Ì0␀␀␀␀␀©Ô0␀␀␀␀␀øÔ0␀␀␀␀␀y0␀␀␀␀␀BÒ0␀␀␀␀␀Ú0␀␀␀␀␀ÊÛ0␀␀␀␀␀˚Ù0␀␀␀␀␀äı0␀␀␀␀␀f˜0␀␀␀␀␀¯0␀␀␀␀␀—¯0␀␀␀␀␀x˙0␀␀␀␀␀!˚0␀␀␀␀␀Õ˚0␀␀␀␀␀í˝0␀␀␀␀␀C˛0␀␀␀␀␀⁄˛0␀␀␀␀␀cˇ0␀␀␀␀␀˚␀1␀␀␀␀␀f1␀␀␀␀␀M1␀␀␀␀␀œ1␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀¢1␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀™1␀␀␀␀␀I1␀␀␀␀␀„1␀␀␀␀␀Ã1␀␀␀␀␀i1␀␀␀␀␀Ç1␀␀␀␀␀á
